hadiths[1243]{hadithnumber,text}:
"5499","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The water of the sea is purifying."""
"5500","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The man's fluid is white and the woman's fluid is yellow. When the two come together and the man's fluid prevails over the woman's fluid, the child is a boy by the permission of Allah, and when the woman's fluid prevails over the man's fluid, it is a girl by the permission of Allah."""
"5501","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The man's fluid is thick and white and the woman's fluid is thin and yellow; whichever of them comes first, the child resembles that one."""
"5502","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Zamzam water benefits according to the intention for which it is drunk."""
"5503","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whatever Allah gives you from the wealth of the ruler, without your asking for it and without your coveting it, eat it and make it your own property."""
"5504","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whatever Allah gives you of this wealth, without your asking for it and without your coveting it, take it; make it your own property or give it in charity. And whatever is not like that, do not let your heart pursue it."""
"5505","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""He has not believed in me who goes to sleep with his stomach full while his neighbour beside him is hungry, and he knows about it."""
"5506","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""No people gather and then disperse without remembering Allah and sending blessings upon the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), except that they rise from a gathering more foul-smelling than a rotting carcass."""
"5507","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""No people gather for remembrance (dhikr) and then disperse from it, except that it is said to them: 'Rise, you have been forgiven.'"""
"5508","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""No people gather and then disperse without remembering Allah, except that it is as though they have dispersed from the carcass of a donkey, and that gathering will be a cause of regret for them."""
"5509","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""No people gather in one of the houses of Allah, reciting the Book of Allah and studying it together among themselves, except that tranquillity descends upon them, mercy covers them, the angels surround them, and Allah mentions them among those who are with Him."""
"5510","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""No people gather in a gathering and then disperse without remembering Allah and sending blessings upon the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), except that their gathering will be a loss and a cause of regret for them on the Day of Resurrection."""
"5511","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I do not find for him from this military expedition of his, in this world or the Hereafter, anything except the dinars that he stipulated."""
"5512","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I would not like the mountain of Uhud to be turned into gold for me and for a single dinar of it to remain with me for more than three days, except a dinar that I keep aside for paying a debt."""
"5513","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I would not like to have gold equal to the mountain of Uhud and for three days to pass over me while any of it is still with me, except something that I keep aside for repaying a debt."""
"5514","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I do not like to greet a man with salam while he is praying, and if he greets me with salam, I will reply to him."""
"5515","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I would not like to imitate any person, even if I were to be given such and such in return for it."""
"5516","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""No servant loves another servant for the sake of Allah except that he has honoured his Lord."""
"5517","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no one who has done me a greater favour than Abu Bakr. He supported me with his own self and his wealth, and he gave me his daughter in marriage."""
"5518","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""No one increases in usury (riba) except that the end of his affair leads to decrease."""
"5519","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""No one who enters Paradise would like to return to the world, even if everything on earth were his, except the martyr; because of the honour he sees, he will wish that he could return and be killed ten times."""
"5520","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whatever a son or a father acquires (of inheritance) belongs to his agnatic heirs ('asabah), whoever they may be."""
"5521","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""No vein twitches and no eye twitches except because of a sin, and what Allah wards off from him is far more."""
"5522","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The world has taken from the Hereafter no more than what a needle takes of the water of the sea when it is dipped into it."""
"5523","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I do not fear poverty for you; rather, I fear for you the race for abundance. And I do not fear mistakes for you; rather, I fear for you deliberate sinning."""
"5524","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I do not know whether Tubba' was a prophet or not. And I do not know whether Dhul-Qarnayn was a prophet or not. And I do not know whether the prescribed punishments (hudud) are an expiation for those upon whom they are carried out or not."""
"5525","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah has not listened to anything as He listens to a prophet with a beautiful voice who recites the Qur'an melodiously and aloud."""
"5526","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I see the matter as coming even sooner than that."""
"5527","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever eats with his servant, rides a donkey in the marketplaces, and holds a goat and milks it himself is not arrogant."""
"5528","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Pray the morning (Fajr) prayer when the light has spread, for it brings a greater reward."""
"5529","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whatever of the lower garment is below the ankles is in the Fire."""
"5530","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whatever intoxicates in large quantity, a small quantity of it is also forbidden."""
"5531","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whatever intoxicates in the amount of a faraq (a large measure), even a handful of it is forbidden."""
"5532","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whatever payment the cupper receives, feed it as fodder to the camel."""
"5533","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whatever game is struck by its sharp edge, eat it; and whatever is struck by its broad side and killed, it is 'waqidh' (killed by a blow), so do not eat it."""
"5534","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Never have I risen on any morning except that I seek forgiveness from Allah Almighty in it one hundred times."""
"5535","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whatever you feed your wife is charity for you, whatever you feed your child is charity for you, whatever you feed your servant is charity for you, and whatever you feed yourself is also charity for you."""
"5536","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""How pure a city you are, and how beloved you are to me! Had my people not driven me out of you, I would not have lived anywhere other than you."" (He said this to Makkah.)"
"5537","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Neither has the sky shaded, nor has the earth carried, anyone more truthful of tongue than Abu Dharr."""
"5538","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Neither has the sky shaded, nor has the earth carried, anyone more truthful of tongue or more faithful than Abu Dharr. He resembles Isa, son of Maryam."""
"5539","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I do not think that so-and-so and so-and-so know anything of our religion."""
"5540","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whatever a man gives to his wife is charity."""
"5541","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""No household is granted gentleness except that it benefits them."""
"5542","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I neither give you nor withhold from you of my own accord; I am only a distributor, placing things where I am commanded."""
"5543","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah has made the Fire forbidden for any servant whose feet become dusty in the path of Allah."""
"5544","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A house in which there is vinegar is not without a condiment."""
"5545","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whenever a man declares another man a disbeliever, it returns to one of the two of them."""
"5546","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""No one has ever eaten any food better than eating from the earnings of his own hands, and the Prophet of Allah Dawud used to eat from the earnings of his own hands."""
"5547","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The world, in comparison with the Hereafter, is only like one of you going to the sea and putting his finger into it; then whatever comes out clinging to that finger, that is the world."""
"5548","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""No deed done on any days is more excellent than the deed done in the first ten days of Dhul-Hijjah, nor is jihad in the path of Allah more excellent than it, except for a man who goes out risking his life and his wealth and does not come back with any of it."""
"5549","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The one being asked about the Hour does not know more than the one asking, but I will tell you its signs: when a slave woman gives birth to her mistress, that is one of its signs; when the barefoot and naked become the leaders of the people, that is one of its signs; and when the herders of goats compete with one another in constructing tall buildings, that is one of its signs. The knowledge of the Hour is among five things of the unseen which no one knows except Allah: 'Indeed, with Allah alone is the knowledge of the Hour.'"""
"5550","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I have not been commanded to build the mosques high and strong."""
"5551","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I have not been commanded to perform ablution every time I urinate, and if I were to do so, it would become a Sunnah."""
"5552","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whatever I command you to do, adopt it, and whatever I forbid you from, refrain from it."""
"5553","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Eat the game that it holds back for you."""
"5554","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""It was not I who gave you mounts to ride; rather, it was Allah who gave you mounts. And by Allah, if Allah wills, whenever I swear an oath and then see something else better than it, I make expiation for my oath and do that which is better."""
"5555","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""What have I to do with the world, and what have I to do with garments decorated with patterns?"""
"5556","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""You do not hear what I am saying any better than they do, except that they are unable to give me any reply."""
"5557","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Compared with those who will come to me at the Pond, you are not even one part out of a hundred thousand parts."""
"5558","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah has not sent down any disease without also sending down its remedy with it."""
"5559","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah has not sent down any disease without also sending down its cure with it."""
"5560","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah has not sent down in the Torah or in the Gospel anything like Umm al-Qur'an (the Mother of the Qur'an); it is al-Sab' al-Mathani (the seven oft-repeated verses), it is divided between Me and My servant, and My servant shall have what he has asked for."""
"5561","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah has not sent down any blessing from the sky without a group of people becoming disbelievers in it. Allah sends down rain, and they say: 'It rained because of such-and-such a star.'"""
"5562","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah does not bestow any blessing upon a servant, and he then praises Allah for it, except that this praise is more excellent than that blessing."""
"5563","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah Almighty does not bestow any blessing upon a servant, and he says: 'Alhamdu lillah' (All praise is for Allah), except that what he has given is more excellent than what he has received."""
"5564","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whatever your heart finds objectionable, leave it."""
"5565","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whatever instrument makes the blood flow, and the name of Allah has been mentioned over it, eat it, except for the tooth and the nail, and I will tell you the reason for that: as for the tooth, it is a bone, and as for the nail, it is the knife of the Abyssinians."""
"5566","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I neither give you anything of my own accord nor withhold it from you; I am only a treasurer, placing things where I am commanded."""
"5567","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""No one has been made to suffer as much harm as I have been made to suffer."""
"5568","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""No one has been made to suffer as much harm in the path of Allah as I have been made to suffer."""
"5569","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Never does anyone call out the Talbiyah, nor does anyone proclaim the Takbir, except that he is given glad tidings of Paradise."""
"5570","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""What is the matter with one of you, that he stands facing his Lord and then spits in front of Him?! Would he like someone to stand facing him and spit in his face? So when one of you wishes to spit, let him spit to his left or beneath his foot, and if he cannot find even that, then let him do like this (that is, in his garment)."""
"5571","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""What is the matter with some people that today they went beyond all limits in killing, until they even killed the children? Beware! The best among you are the children of the polytheists. Listen! Do not kill children. Listen! Do not kill children. Every child is born upon the fitrah (natural disposition) and remains upon it until its tongue begins to express itself; then its parents make it a Jew or a Christian."""
"5572","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""What is the matter with some people that they say such-and-such? Yet I pray and I also sleep, I fast and I also break my fast, and I also marry women. So whoever turns away from my way is not of me."""
"5573","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""What is the matter with some people that they keep away from something that I do?! By Allah, I am the one among them who knows Allah best and fears Him most."""
"5574","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""What is the matter with some people that they raise their eyes towards the sky during their prayer?! They must certainly stop doing that, or else their eyesight will be snatched away."""
"5575","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""What is the matter with those who move their hands about in prayer as though they were the tails of restive horses? Is it not sufficient for one of you to place his hand on his thigh and give the salam to his right and his left?"""
"5576","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""What is the matter with some men that they practise wisal (continuous fasting without breaking the fast)?! You are not like me. Listen! By Allah, if the month were prolonged for me, I would practise such wisal that those who go to extremes would abandon their extremism."""
"5577","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah did not send any prophet except that he warned his nation about the Dajjal. Nuh and all the prophets after him warned about him. He will certainly emerge among you, and whatever of his affair may remain hidden from you, it will not be hidden from you that your Lord is not one-eyed, whereas the Dajjal will be blind in the right eye, as though his eye were a protruding grape. Listen! Allah has made your blood and your wealth sacred to you just like the sanctity of this day of yours, in this city of yours, in this month of yours. Beware! Have I conveyed the message? O Allah, be witness (he said this three times). Woe to you! Look, do not become disbelievers after me, striking the necks of one another."""
"5578","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah did not send any prophet except that he warned his nation about the one-eyed, lying Dajjal. Listen! He is one-eyed, and your Lord is not one-eyed. Between his two eyes will be written 'Kafir' (disbeliever), which every believer will read."""
"5579","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah has not sent any prophet, nor appointed any caliph, except that he has two inner circles: one circle that commands him to do good and urges him towards it, and one circle that commands him to do evil and urges him towards it. The one who is protected is only the one whom Allah protects."""
"5580","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah has not sent any prophet, nor has there been any caliph after him, except that he has two inner circles: one circle that commands him to do good and forbids him from evil, and one circle that spares no effort in bringing ruin upon him. So whoever is saved from the evil circle has truly been saved."""
"5581","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah did not send any prophet except that he herded goats, and I too used to herd the goats of the people of Makkah for a few qirats."""
"5582","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Wealth that reaches the limit on which zakah is to be paid, and its zakah has been paid, is not a hoarded treasure."""
"5583","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""What is between the navel and the knee is 'awrah (the part that must be covered)."""
"5584","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""What lies between the east and the west is qiblah."""
"5585","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Between the two blowings of the Trumpet there is an interval of forty. Then Allah will send down water from the sky, and people will sprout as vegetation sprouts. There is nothing of a human being that does not decay, except one bone, and that is the end of the spine (the tailbone); from it he was created, and from it the whole creature will be reassembled on the Day of Resurrection."""
"5586","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""What is between my house and my pulpit is one of the gardens of Paradise."""
"5587","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""What is between my house and my pulpit is one of the gardens of Paradise, and my pulpit is upon my Pond."""
"5588","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""From the creation of Adam until the establishment of the Hour, there is no matter greater than the Dajjal."""
"5589","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The area between the two stony plains of Madinah is sacred (inviolable)."""
"5590","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Between two of the door-leaves of Paradise is a distance of forty years' travel, and a day will surely come upon it when it will be packed with the multitude of people."""
"5591","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The distance between the two shoulders of the disbeliever in Hell will be three days' journey for a fast rider."""
"5592","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The distance between the two sides of my Pond is like that between Sana'a and Madinah, or like that between Madinah and Amman. You will see in it jugs of gold and silver as numerous as the stars of the sky, or even more."""
"5593","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""What are you asking me to do?! Are you asking me to tell him to leave his hand in your mouth so that you can chew it up as a male camel chews?! Put your hand in his mouth until he bites it, then pull it out."""
"5594","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whenever two people love one another for the sake of Allah Almighty, the better of the two is the one who has greater love for his companion."""
"5595","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whatever part of the lower garment is below the ankles is in the Fire."""
"5596","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Every step the pilgrim's camel lifts and every foot it puts down, Allah Almighty writes in return for it a good deed for him, or erases a sin from him, or raises him a degree."""
"5597","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I have not left behind me any trial (fitnah) more harmful to men than women."""
"5598","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""What do you want from Ali? What do you want from Ali? What do you want from Ali? Indeed, Ali is from me and I am from him, and he is the friend (wali) of every believer after me."""
"5599","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When the sun rises high, nothing of Allah's creation remains but that it glorifies Allah with His praise, except the devils and the foolish among the children of Adam."""
"5600","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whenever anyone gives charity from pure earnings, and Allah accepts nothing but what is pure, the Most Merciful accepts it with His right hand; and even if it is a single date, it keeps growing in the palm of the Most Merciful until it becomes greater than a mountain, just as one of you raises his foal or his young camel."""
"5601","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""What are you saying? If it is a matter of your worldly affairs, then it is your own business; and if it is a matter of your religion, then it is to be referred to me."""
"5602","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whom do you consider a martyr among you?"" The Companions said: ""Being killed in the path of Allah."" He said: ""In that case the martyrs of my Ummah would be very few. Whoever is killed in the path of Allah is a martyr, whoever dies in the path of Allah is also a martyr, the one who dies of a stomach disease is a martyr, the one who dies of the plague is a martyr, and the one who dies by drowning is a martyr."""
"5603","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whenever two people love one another for the sake of Allah, separation comes between them only because of a sin that one of them commits."""
"5604","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whenever a Muslim man makes the mosques his dwelling for prayer and the remembrance of Allah, Allah rejoices over him from the moment he leaves his house, just as a family rejoices over their traveller when he returns to them."""
"5605","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah never took the soul of any prophet except that he was buried where his soul was taken."""
"5606","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whenever Allah decrees a servant's death in a land, He also places some need for him there."""
"5607","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whenever people sit in a gathering in which they neither remember Allah Almighty nor send blessings upon their Prophet, it will be a cause of loss for them; then, if Allah wills, He will punish them, and if He wills, He will forgive them."""
"5608","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whenever people sit to remember Allah, the angels surround them, mercy covers them, tranquillity (sakinah) descends upon them, and Allah mentions them among those who are with Him."""
"5609","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whenever people sit to remember Allah Almighty, a caller calls out to them from the heavens: 'Rise, you have been forgiven.'"""
"5610","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whenever people sit to remember Allah Almighty and then rise, it is said to them: 'Rise, Allah has forgiven you your sins and your evil deeds have been changed into good deeds.'"""
"5611","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whatever troubles your heart, leave it."""
"5612","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The sun has never been held back for any human being except for Yusha' bin Nun, during the nights when he marched towards Bayt al-Maqdis."""
"5613","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Jews have not envied you for anything as much as they have envied you for the salam and for saying 'Amin'."""
"5614","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""It is not right for a Muslim man who has something about which he wishes to make a bequest to spend two nights without having his will written down with him."""
"5615","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""It is not right for a Muslim man who has something about which he wishes to make a bequest to spend three nights without having his will written down with him."""
"5616","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whenever the dust of the path of Allah enters the heart of a Muslim man, Allah makes the Fire unlawful for him."""
"5617","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whenever a man leaves his house seeking knowledge, Allah makes easy for him a path to Paradise."""
"5618","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whatever garment is behind (below) the ankles is in the Fire."""
"5619","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whenever Ammar was given a choice between two matters, he chose the more correct of them."""
"5620","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Two hungry wolves let loose among a flock of sheep do not ruin it as much as a man's greed for wealth and status ruins his religion."""
"5621","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I have never seen anything like today in good and evil. Today Paradise and Hell were shown to me, until I saw them behind this wall."""
"5622","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I have not seen anything like the Fire, from which the one fleeing it still sleeps, nor anything like Paradise, whose seeker still sleeps."""
"5623","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I have never seen any sight except that the grave is more terrifying than it."""
"5624","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Despite being deficient in intellect and religion, I have not seen anyone more able than you women to overcome a man of sound understanding. As for the deficiency in intellect, it is that the testimony of two women equals the testimony of one man; and as for the deficiency in religion, it is that one of you leaves off fasting in Ramadan and spends several days without praying."""
"5625","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""We did not find any cause for alarm, and we found this horse as swift as the sea."""
"5626","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""No servant has been given anything better or more expansive than patience."""
"5627","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""What you were doing continued in this way until I feared that this prayer would be made obligatory upon you, and had it been made obligatory upon you, you would not have kept it up. So, O people, pray in your homes, for the best prayer of a man is in his home, except the obligatory prayer."""
"5628","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Jibril kept urging me to treat the neighbour well until I thought that he would make him an heir."""
"5629","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The poisoned meat I ate at Khaybar kept returning to affect me every year, until now is the time when my aorta is about to be severed."""
"5630","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whenever a Muslim man asks Allah for Paradise three times, Paradise says: 'O Allah, admit him into Paradise.' And whenever a Muslim man seeks Allah's protection from Hell three times, Hell says: 'O Allah, protect him from me.'"""
"5631","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""What is the matter with you, that you gesture with your hands as though they were the tails of unruly horses?! When one of you says the salam at the end of the prayer, let him turn towards his companions and not gesture with his hand."""
"5632","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Nothing will be heavier in the scale of the believer on the Day of Resurrection than good character. Indeed, Allah Almighty hates the shameless, foul-mouthed person."""
"5633","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whenever a people went astray after having been upon guidance, they had been given to argumentation."""
"5634","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whenever usury (riba) and fornication spread among a people, they make themselves deserving of the punishment of Allah."""
"5635","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no harm for any of you, if he has the means, to have two special garments made for the day of Jumu'ah, besides his work clothes."""
"5636","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever on earth says 'La ilaha illallahu wallahu akbar, wa la hawla wa la quwwata illa billah' (There is none worthy of worship except Allah, Allah is the Greatest, and there is no power to avoid sin and no strength to do good except by the enabling of Allah), his sins are forgiven, even if they are like the foam of the sea."""
"5637","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whenever any Muslim on earth asks Allah for something in supplication, Allah grants it to him or averts from him an equal amount of evil, as long as he does not supplicate for sin or for severing family ties, and as long as he is not hasty, saying: 'I supplicated a great deal, but my supplication was not answered.'"""
"5638","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no soul on earth that dies having good with Allah that would like to return to you, even if the whole world were given to it, except the one killed in the path of Allah; seeing the reward Allah has for him, he would like to return and be killed once again."""
"5639","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Of all the souls that have been born on earth as of today, not one will see a hundred years pass over it."""
"5640","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no oath on earth that I swear and then see something else better than it, except that I do what is better."""
"5641","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I did not teach him anything when he was ignorant, nor did I feed him when he was hungry."""
"5642","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""What harm would there have been for her had she made use of its skin? Allah has only made eating it unlawful."""
"5643","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no harm upon you if you do not practise withdrawal (azl), for Allah has decreed whatever He is to create until the Day of Resurrection."""
"5644","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A man has not done any deed that saves him from the punishment of Allah more than the remembrance of Allah."""
"5645","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The son of Adam has not done any deed more virtuous than prayer, reconciliation between people, and good character."""
"5646","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whenever a man opens a door of giving through charity or maintaining ties of kinship, Allah Almighty grants him further abundance through it; and whenever a man opens a door of begging, intending abundance by it, Allah Almighty afflicts him with further scarcity through it."""
"5647","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no tree in Paradise except that its trunk is of gold."""
"5648","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whenever a servant says 'La ilaha illallah' (There is no true god except Allah) with sincerity, the gates of the heaven are opened for him until they reach the Throne, provided that he avoids the major sins."""
"5649","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah Almighty did not take the soul of any prophet except in the very place where he loved to be buried."""
"5650","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whatever soul Allah has decreed to create will certainly come into existence."""
"5651","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whatever has been decreed in the womb will certainly come to be."""
"5652","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whatever part is cut off from an animal while it is alive is carrion."""
"5653","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""What is little and suffices is better than much that causes heedlessness."""
"5654","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Gentleness is not in anything except that it beautifies it, and it is not removed from anything except that it makes it ugly."""
"5655","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Obscenity is not in anything except that it makes it ugly, and modesty is not in anything except that it beautifies it."""
"5656","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whatever pact was made in the Jahiliyyah (pre-Islamic period of ignorance), hold firmly to it, and no new pact is to be made in Islam."""
"5657","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whatever inheritance was divided in the Jahiliyyah (pre-Islamic period of ignorance) shall remain according to the division of the Jahiliyyah, and whatever inheritance remained undivided until Islam came shall be divided according to the division of Islam."""
"5658","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whatever lost item is found on a public road or in an inhabited town, announce it for one year; then if its owner comes, give it to him, and if he does not come, it is yours. And whatever is found in a ruin, then in it and in buried treasure (rikaz) there is one-fifth."""
"5659","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whatever you would dislike people to see from you, do not do it yourself when you are alone."""
"5660","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A man has not earned any earning better than the work of his own hands, and whatever a man spends on himself, his family, his children and his servant is charity."""
"5661","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no one, apart from Abu Bakr, who has done us a favour except that we have repaid him for it. As for Abu Bakr, he has done us a favour for which Allah will repay him on the Day of Resurrection. The wealth of no one has ever benefited me as much as the wealth of Abu Bakr has benefited me. If I were to take anyone as an intimate friend (khalil), I would have taken Abu Bakr as an intimate friend. Listen! Your companion is the intimate friend (khalil) of Allah."""
"5662","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""What is the matter with this child of yours that he is crying? Why did you not have ruqyah done for him against the evil eye?"""
"5663","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""What good is there for you in sitting in the roads? Avoid sitting in the roads. And if you must sit, then give them their right: lowering the gaze, returning the greeting of salam, guiding the way, and speaking good words."""
"5664","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""What is the matter that I see upon you the ornament of the people of Hell (that is, an iron ring)?"""
"5665","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""What is the matter that I see you raising your hands as though they were the tails of unruly horses? Be still in prayer."""
"5666","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""What is the matter that I see you in separate groups?"""
"5667","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""What is the matter that I saw you clapping so much? Whoever is faced with something in his prayer should say 'Subhan Allah' (Glory be to Allah), for when he says 'Subhan Allah', attention will be turned to him. Clapping is only for women."""
"5668","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""What have I to do with this world! I am in this world only like a traveller who takes shade under a tree, then moves on and leaves it."""
"5669","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""What have I to do with this world, and what has this world to do with me! By the One in whose Hand is my soul, the likeness of me and this world is only like that of a traveller who journeys on a hot summer day, then takes shade under a tree for an hour of the day, then moves on and leaves it."""
"5670","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""No prophet died except that he was buried where his soul was taken."""
"5671","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""On the night I was taken on the Night Journey (Mi'raj), I did not pass by any group of angels except that they said: 'O Muhammad, command your Ummah to have cupping (hijamah).'"""
"5672","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""On the night I was taken on the Night Journey (Mi'raj), I did not pass by any group of angels except that all of them would say to me: 'O Muhammad, hold firmly to cupping (hijamah).'"""
"5673","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whatever thing Allah Almighty transformed (into another form), it had no progeny or offspring that continued."""
"5674","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A human being has not filled any vessel worse than his stomach. It is sufficient for the son of Adam to have a few morsels that keep his back upright. If it must be (more), then let him leave one third for his food, one third for his drink and one third for his breath."""
"5675","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no human being except that there is a bridle in his head held in the hand of an angel. When he humbles himself, it is said to the angel: 'Raise his bridle,' and when he behaves arrogantly, it is said to the angel: 'Let go of his bridle.'"""
"5676","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever does not pay the zakah on his wealth, on the Day of Resurrection it will be made to appear to him as a bald snake, until it becomes a collar around his neck."""
"5677","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever takes a loan while Allah knows that he intends to repay it, Allah has it repaid on his behalf in this very world."""
"5678","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever makes a supplication, Allah gives him what he asked for or averts from him an equivalent amount of evil, as long as he does not supplicate for sin or for severing ties of kinship."""
"5679","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever greets me with salam, Allah returns my soul to me so that I return his greeting of salam."""
"5680","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whenever forty believers seek forgiveness for a believer, Allah accepts their intercession for him."""
"5681","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no prophet among the prophets except that he was given signs the like of which people believed in. What I have been given is revelation that Allah has revealed to me, so I hope that I will have the most followers of them all on the Day of Resurrection."""
"5682","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no heart among hearts except that a cloud like the cloud of the moon comes over it: just as the moon is shining, then suddenly a cloud covers it and it becomes dark, then the cloud clears away."""
"5683","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whichever Muslim among the people has three children die before reaching puberty, Allah will admit him into Paradise by the bounty of His mercy towards them."""
"5684","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no Muslim soul among the people whose Lord takes it and which would love to return to you, even if it were given the world and everything in it, except the martyrs. And that I be killed in the path of Allah is more beloved to me than that I should have the wealth of the people of tents and houses."""
"5685","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no ruler or governor who closes his door to the needy, the destitute and the poor except that Allah will close the gates of the heaven to his need, his want and his poverty."""
"5686","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no Muslim man who, when an obligatory prayer comes due, performs its ablution, its humility and its bowing well, except that it becomes an expiation for the sins before it, as long as no major sin is committed; and that is for all time."""
"5687","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no Muslim man who visits a sick Muslim except that Allah sends seventy thousand angels who keep invoking blessings upon him: if it is at any hour of the day, until evening, and if it is at any hour of the night, until morning."""
"5688","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no Muslim man who cleans barley for his horse and then hangs it on it except that Allah records for him a good deed for every grain."""
"5689","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no man who performs ablution and does it well, then prays, except that the sins between that prayer and the next prayer are forgiven for him until he prays it."""
"5690","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no man who abandons a Muslim in a situation where his honour is being attacked and his sanctity violated, except that Allah Almighty will abandon him in a situation where he would love to be helped. And there is no one who helps a Muslim in a situation where his honour is being attacked and his sanctity violated, except that Allah will help him in a situation where he would love to be helped."""
"5691","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no man who has a regular prayer at night and is overcome by sleep, except that Allah Almighty records for him the reward of his prayer, and his sleep becomes a charity for him."""
"5692","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no woman who removes her clothes anywhere other than her own home except that she has torn the veil between herself and Allah."""
"5693","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no nation except that part of it will be in Hell and part of it in Paradise, except my nation, for all of it will be in Paradise."""
"5694","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no ruler except that he has two inner circles from among his own people: one circle that enjoins him to do good and forbids him from evil, and one circle that spares no effort to bring him harm. So whoever is protected from its evil has truly been protected, and he becomes like whichever of the two prevails over him."""
"5695","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no leader appointed over ten people except that he will be brought on the Day of Resurrection bound, then his justice will release him or his oppression will destroy him."""
"5696","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no leader appointed over ten people except that he will be brought on the Day of Resurrection in such a state that his hand is tied to his neck."""
"5697","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no ruler who takes charge of the affairs of the Muslims and then does not strive for them and act sincerely for their good, except that he will not enter Paradise with them."""
"5698","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no household to whom a plough comes in the morning except that they are humiliated."""
"5699","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no camel except that on its hump there is a devil. So when you ride it, remember this blessing of Allah Almighty as Allah has commanded you, then put it to use for your own work, for in reality it is Allah Almighty who carries you."""
"5700","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""No child of the children of Adam is born except that Satan touches him at the time of his birth, so he cries out screaming from the touch of Satan, except Maryam and her son."""
"5701","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There are no three people in a village or in the desert among whom the prayer is not established in congregation except that Satan gains mastery over them. So hold fast to the congregation, for the wolf only eats the sheep that strays from the flock."""
"5702","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no one who goes out of his house in pursuit of knowledge except that the angels spread their wings for him, pleased with what he is doing, until he returns."""
"5703","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no supplication a servant makes that is more excellent than this supplication: 'Allahumma inni as'aluka al-mu'afata fid-dunya wal-akhirah' (O Allah, I ask You for well-being in this world and the Hereafter)."""
"5704","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no sin more deserving that Allah Almighty should hasten its punishment for His servant in this world, along with what He stores up for him in the Hereafter, than oppression and severing the ties of kinship."""
"5705","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no sin more deserving that Allah Almighty should hasten its punishment for His servant in this world, along with what He stores up for him in the Hereafter, than severing the ties of kinship, betrayal and lying. And indeed, the act of obedience whose reward comes the quickest is maintaining the ties of kinship, so much so that the members of a household, despite being sinful, see their wealth grow and their numbers increase when they maintain the ties of kinship with one another."""
"5706","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no rider who, alone on his journey, occupies himself with Allah and His remembrance except that an angel rides behind him; and whoever, alone, occupies himself with poetry and the like, a devil rides behind him."""
"5707","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no man who has wealth and does not pay the due of his wealth except that a collar will be made for him around his neck; it will be a bald snake. He will flee from it and the snake will pursue him."""
"5708","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no Muslim man who dies and forty men who do not associate anything with Allah stand over his funeral, except that Allah accepts their intercession for him."""
"5709","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no Muslim man three of whose children die before reaching puberty except that Allah will admit him into Paradise by the grace of His mercy towards them."""
"5710","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no man who purifies himself on Friday as he has been commanded, then goes out of his house and comes to the Friday prayer, and remains silent until its prayer is completed, except that this becomes an expiation for what came before it, up to the previous Friday."""
"5711","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no man who considers himself great and walks with arrogance except that he will meet Allah Almighty while He is angry with him."""
"5712","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no man who suffers a wound in his body and then gives it in charity except that Allah removes from him sins equal to what he gave in charity."""
"5713","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no man who knows some knowledge and then conceals it except that on the Day of Resurrection he will be brought bridled with a bridle of fire."""
"5714","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no man who makes a supplication except that his supplication is answered: either it is given to him quickly in this world, or it is stored up for him in the Hereafter, as long as he does not supplicate for a sin or for severing the ties of kinship, or become hasty, saying: 'I supplicated to my Lord, but He did not answer me.'"""
"5715","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no man who travels a path in which he seeks knowledge except that Allah makes easy for him the path to Paradise. And whoever is held back by his deeds, his lineage will not bring him forward."""
"5716","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no man over whom a hundred people offer the funeral prayer except that he is forgiven."""
"5717","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no man who visits a sick person in the evening except that seventy thousand angels go out with him, seeking forgiveness for him until the morning; and whoever comes to him in the morning, seventy thousand angels go out with him, seeking forgiveness for him until the evening."""
"5718","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no man who takes charge of the affairs of ten people or more except that he will come to Allah with his hand tied to his neck; then his righteousness will release him or his sin will bind him further. Its beginning is blame, its middle is regret, and its end is disgrace on the Day of Resurrection."""
"5719","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no man who does not pay the zakah on his wealth except that on the Day of Resurrection Allah will place a bald snake around his neck. And whoever seizes the wealth of his Muslim brother by means of a false oath will meet Allah while He is angry with him."""
"5720","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""No hour passes over the son of Adam in which he did not remember Allah except that he will regret it on the Day of Resurrection."""
"5721","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is nothing in the Scale heavier than good character."""
"5722","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is nothing that I had not been shown before except that I have seen it while standing in this very place of mine, even Paradise and Hell. And it has been revealed to me that you will be tested in your graves like, or close to, the trial of the False Messiah (al-Masih al-Dajjal). Angels will come to each one of you and he will be asked: 'What do you know about this man?' As for the believer, or the one with certainty, he will say: 'He is Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah; he came to us with clear proofs and guidance, so we responded, believed and followed him. He is Muhammad' (he will say this three times). Then it will be said to him: 'Sleep in righteousness; we knew that you were certain of him.' As for the hypocrite, or the doubter, he will say: 'I do not know; I heard the people saying something, so I said it too.'"""
"5723","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whatever affliction befalls the believer, even a thorn that pricks him, Allah records for him a good deed on account of it and removes from him a sin because of it."""
"5724","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whatever befalls the believer in his body that hurts him, Allah expiates his sins through it."""
"5725","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whatever befalls the believer of fatigue, grief or illness, even a worry that troubles him, Allah expiates his sins through it."""
"5726","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is nothing placed in the Scale heavier than good character, and the person of good character, by means of it, reaches the rank of the one who fasts and prays."""
"5727","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no owner of camels, cattle or sheep who does not pay their zakah except that they will come on the Day of Resurrection larger and fatter than they ever were. They will butt him with their horns and trample him with their hooves; whenever the last of them passes, the first of them will return to him again, until judgment is passed between the people."""
"5728","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no owner of camels who does not fulfil their due except that they will come on the Day of Resurrection more numerous than they ever were, and he will be made to sit for them in a level plain, and they will trample him with their legs and hooves. And there is no owner of cattle who does not fulfil their due except that they will come on the Day of Resurrection more numerous than they ever were, and he will be made to sit for them in a level plain, and they will butt him with their horns and trample him with their legs. Nor is there an owner of sheep who does not fulfil their due except that they will come on the Day of Resurrection more numerous than they ever were, and he will be made to sit for them in a level plain, and they will butt him with their horns and trample him with their hooves; among them there will be none without horns and none with a broken horn. Nor is there an owner of treasure who does not fulfil its due except that his treasure will come on the Day of Resurrection in the form of a bald snake, pursuing him with its mouth wide open. When it comes to him, he will flee from it. Then his Lord, the Mighty and Majestic, will call out to him: 'Take your treasure which you hid away, for I am free of need of you.' Then, when he sees that there is no escape for him from it, he will put his hand into its mouth, and it will chew it the way a male camel chews."""
"5729","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no owner of gold or silver who does not pay its due from it except that, when the Day of Resurrection comes, plates of fire will be made for him, then they will be heated in the fire of Hell, and his side, his forehead and his back will be branded with them. Whenever they cool, they will be heated again and returned to him, on a Day whose length is fifty thousand years, until judgment is passed between the servants; then he will be shown his way, either to Paradise or to the Fire. Nor is there an owner of camels who does not pay their due from them, and part of their due is that they be milked on the day they come to water, except that, when the Day of Resurrection comes, he will be laid flat for them in a level plain, with them at their most numerous, not a single young camel missing from them. They will trample him with their hooves and bite him with their mouths; whenever the first of them passes over him, the last of them will be brought back over him, on a Day whose length is fifty thousand years, until judgment is passed between the servants; then he will be shown his way, either to Paradise or to the Fire. Nor is there an owner of cattle or sheep who does not pay their due from them except that, when the Day of Resurrection comes, he will be laid flat for them in a level plain, with nothing missing from them; among them there will be none with twisted horns, none without horns and none with a broken horn. They will butt him with their horns and trample him with their hooves; whenever the first of them passes over him, the last of them will be brought back over him, on a Day whose length is fifty thousand years, until judgment is passed between the servants; then he will be shown his way, either to Paradise or to the Fire."""
"5730","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no obligatory prayer except that there are two units (rak'ahs) before it."""
"5731","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no year except that the one after it will be worse than it, until you meet your Lord."""
"5732","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no servant except that he has a reputation in the heavens. If his reputation in the heavens is good, it is placed on the earth as well; and if his reputation in the heavens is bad, that too is placed on the earth."""
"5733","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no servant who says 'La ilaha illallah' (There is no true god except Allah) and then dies upon that except that he will enter Paradise, even if he committed adultery and even if he stole, even if he committed adultery and even if he stole, even if the nose of Abu Dharr be rubbed in the dust."""
"5734","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no servant who has the intention of repaying his debt except that he receives help from Allah."""
"5735","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no believing servant except that he has a sin that he falls into every now and then, or a sin that he persists in and does not leave until he leaves this world. Indeed, the believer was created prone to trial, oft-repenting and forgetful; when he is reminded, he remembers."""
"5736","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no Muslim servant who performs ablution and does it thoroughly, then prays for Allah every day twelve units (rak'ahs) of voluntary prayer besides the obligatory, except that Allah builds for him a house in Paradise."""
"5737","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no Muslim servant who supplicates for his brother in his absence except that the angel says: 'And for you the like of it.'"""
"5738","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no servant who commits a sin, then performs ablution and completes it well, then stands and prays two units (rak'ahs), then seeks Allah's forgiveness for that sin, except that Allah forgives him."""
"5739","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no servant who raises his hands and asks Allah for something except that Allah grants it to him, as long as he does not become hasty, saying: 'I asked and asked, but I was not given anything.'"""
"5740","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no servant whom Allah places in charge of a flock of people, and who on the day he dies is deceiving his flock, except that Allah forbids Paradise to him."""
"5741","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no servant who makes a single prostration for Allah except that Allah raises him by one degree because of it and removes from him one sin."""
"5742","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no servant who makes a single prostration for Allah except that Allah records for him a good deed because of it, removes from him a sin and raises him by one degree. So prostrate abundantly."""
"5743","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no servant who is struck down by an illness except that Allah raises him up from it purified."""
"5744","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no servant who sends blessings (salah) upon me except that the angels send mercy upon him for as long as he keeps sending blessings upon me. So let the servant do little of it or much."""
"5745","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no servant who says three times every day in the morning and every night in the evening: 'Bismillahil-ladhi la yadurru ma'a ismihi shay'un fil-ardi wa la fis-sama'i wa huwas-Sami'ul-'Alim' (In the name of Allah, with whose name nothing in the earth or in the heaven can cause harm, and He is the All-Hearing, the All-Knowing) and then anything harms him."""
"5746","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no army that fights in the path of Allah and obtains spoils of war except that they have taken two-thirds of their reward of the Hereafter in advance, and one-third remains for them; and if they do not obtain spoils, their full reward is completed for them."""
"5747","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no heart except that it hangs between two of the fingers of the Most Merciful; if He wills He keeps it upright, and if He wills He turns it astray. And the Scale is in the hand of the Most Merciful; He raises some people and lowers others until the Day of Resurrection."""
"5748","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There are no people who remember Allah except that the angels surround them, mercy covers them, tranquility (sakinah) descends upon them, and Allah mentions them among those who are with Him."""
"5749","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no people among whom sins are committed, while they are more powerful and more numerous than those who commit them, and yet they do not change it, except that Allah Almighty envelops them all in punishment because of it."""
"5750","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""People who rise from a gathering in which they did not remember Allah Almighty are as though they have risen from the rotting carcass of a donkey, and that gathering will be a cause of regret for them on the Day of Resurrection."""
"5751","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A child is not born from every (drop of) fluid; and when Allah wills to create something, nothing can prevent Him."""
"5752","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I have the greatest right over every believer in this world and the Hereafter. Recite, if you wish, this verse: 'The Prophet has a greater right over the believers than their own selves.' So whichever believer dies and leaves wealth, his agnatic heirs ('asabah) shall inherit from him, whoever they may be; and whoever leaves a debt or helpless dependants, let him come to me, for I am his guardian (protector)."""
"5753","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever is wounded in the path of Allah - and Allah knows best who is wounded in His path - will come on the Day of Resurrection with his wound just as it was on the day he was wounded: its colour the colour of blood and its scent the scent of musk."""
"5754","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whichever Muslim spends the night in a state of ablution while remembering Allah, then wakes up during the night and asks Allah Almighty for good in any matter of this world and the Hereafter, Allah will certainly grant it to him."""
"5755","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whichever Muslim purifies himself and completes the purification that Allah has made obligatory upon him, then prays these five prayers, these prayers become an expiation for (the sins) between them."""
"5756","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whichever Muslim performs ablution and does his ablution well, then stands and prays two rak'ahs, turning to them fully with his heart and his face, Paradise becomes obligatory for him."""
"5757","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whichever Muslim sows a crop or plants a tree, and then a bird, a human or an animal eats from it, it becomes charity (sadaqah) for him."""
"5758","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whichever Muslim is pricked by a thorn or afflicted by anything greater than it, a rank is recorded for him because of it and a sin of his is erased."""
"5759","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whichever Muslim three people testify for (in his favour), Paradise becomes obligatory for him."" It was said: ""And two?"" He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""And two (are also enough)."""
"5760","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whichever Muslim grows a grey hair in Islam, Allah records a good deed for him because of it and removes a sin from him."""
"5761","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whichever Muslim is afflicted with some hardship in his body, Allah Almighty commands the guardian angels: 'Record for My servant, every day and every night, the same good that he used to do (when healthy), for as long as he remains confined in this bond of Mine (illness).'"""
"5762","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whichever Muslim has the funeral prayer offered over him by an entire community (a large congregation), they intercede for him."""
"5763","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whichever Muslim is afflicted by a thorn or anything greater than it, Allah sheds his sins because of it just as a tree sheds its leaves."""
"5764","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whichever Muslim is struck by a calamity and says what Allah has commanded: 'Inna lillahi wa inna ilayhi raji'un (We belong to Allah and to Him we return). O Allah, reward me in my calamity and give me something better than it in return,' Allah rewards him for his calamity and gives him something better than it in return."""
"5765","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whichever Muslim is wronged, then fights against it and is killed, dies as a martyr."""
"5766","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whichever Muslim visits a sick person whose appointed time (of death) has not yet come, and says seven times: 'I ask Allah the Mighty, the Lord of the Mighty Throne, to cure you,' he (the sick person) will certainly be cured."""
"5767","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whichever Muslim visits a (sick) Muslim in the morning, seventy thousand angels keep praying for mercy for him until the evening; and if he visits him in the evening, seventy thousand angels keep praying for him until the morning; and he will have a garden in Paradise."""
"5768","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whichever Muslim plants a tree, whatever is eaten from it is charity for him, whatever is stolen from it is also charity for him, whatever a wild beast eats is also charity for him, whatever the birds eat is also charity for him, and whatever anyone takes from it is charity for him."""
"5769","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whichever Muslim lends a Muslim a loan twice, it is equal to giving it in charity once."""
"5770","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whichever Muslim calls out the talbiyah, whatever stone, tree or clod of earth is on his right and left also calls out the talbiyah with him, until the earth comes to an end on this side and that side."""
"5771","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whichever Muslim dies and forty men who do not associate anything with Allah stand (in prayer) over his funeral, they intercede for him."""
"5772","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whichever Muslim has three of his children die who had not yet reached puberty, they will receive him at the eight gates of Paradise, and he may enter by whichever of them he wishes."""
"5773","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whichever Muslim dies on the day of Friday or the night of Friday, Allah Almighty protects him from the trial of the grave."""
"5774","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whichever Muslim spends a pair from each kind of his wealth in the path of Allah, all the gatekeepers of Paradise will receive him, each of them calling him towards himself, so that he enters by his gate."""
"5775","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When two Muslims confront each other with their swords, both the killer and the killed will be in the Fire."""
"5776","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whichever two Muslims have three of their children die who had not yet reached puberty, Allah admits both parents into Paradise by the bounty of His mercy towards those children."""
"5777","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When two Muslims meet and shake hands, they are forgiven before they part."""
"5778","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When two Muslims meet, and one of them greets the other with salam and takes hold of his hand, and he takes his hand only for the sake of Allah, they do not part until they are forgiven."""
"5779","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whichever two Muslims have three children between them die who had not yet reached puberty, both of them are forgiven."""
"5780","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whichever two Muslims have three children die who had not yet reached puberty, Allah admits both parents into Paradise by the bounty of His mercy towards those children. It will be said to the children: 'Enter Paradise.' They will say: 'Not until our parents enter (we will not go).' Then it will be said: 'Enter Paradise, you and your parents, all of you.'"""
"5781","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whichever two Muslims have three children die who had not yet reached puberty, Allah admits both of them into Paradise by the bounty of His mercy towards those children."""
"5782","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whatever calamity befalls a Muslim, Allah expiates his sins because of it, even a thorn that pricks him."""
"5783","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever is wounded in the path of Allah will come on the Day of Resurrection with his wound flowing with blood: its colour the colour of blood and its scent the scent of musk."""
"5784","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Every child is born upon the fitrah (natural disposition); then his parents make him a Jew, a Christian or a Magian, just as an animal gives birth to a whole, sound young one. Do you see any part of it cut off?"""
"5785","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Every child that is born is poked by Satan, and it cries out loudly because of Satan's poke, except the son of Maryam and his mother."""
"5786","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whichever deceased person has the funeral prayer offered over him by a congregation of Muslims numbering up to a hundred, and they intercede for him, their intercession for him is accepted."""
"5787","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whichever deceased person has the funeral prayer offered over him by a congregation of people, their intercession for him is accepted."""
"5788","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whichever deceased person dies, and his mourners stand up and say: 'Alas, my mountain! Alas, my support!' or similar words, two angels are appointed over that deceased who strike him, saying: 'Were you really like that?!'"""
"5789","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Every prophet warned his nation about the one-eyed liar (the Dajjal). Beware! He is one-eyed, and your Lord is not one-eyed. Between his eyes is written 'Kafir' (disbeliever)."""
"5790","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There was no prophet whom Allah sent to a nation before me except that he had among his nation special disciples and companions who followed his Sunnah and adhered to his command. Then after them came unworthy successors who said what they did not do and did what they were not commanded. So whoever strives against them with his hand is a believer, whoever strives against them with his tongue is a believer, and whoever strives against them with his heart is a believer; beyond that there is not even a mustard seed's weight of faith."""
"5791","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Every prophet who falls ill is given the choice between this world and the Hereafter."""
"5792","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever dies and has good with Allah would not like to return to this world, even if he were given this world and everything in it, except the martyr; for he wishes to return to this world and be killed (as a martyr) once again, because of the excellence he sees in martyrdom."""
"5793","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever dies in a state where he bears witness to 'La ilaha illallah' (there is no true god except Allah) and that I am the Messenger of Allah, and this testimony comes from a heart that has certainty, Allah forgives him."""
"5794","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""For every soul that is born, Allah has already written its place in Paradise or Hell, and has also written whether it is wretched or blessed."" It was said: ""Should we not then rely on this and give up deeds?"" He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""No, keep doing deeds and do not sit back relying on it, for each person is made easy for that for which he was created. So the deeds of the people of blessedness are made easy for the people of blessedness, and the deeds of the people of wretchedness are made easy for the people of wretchedness."""
"5795","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Every soul that has been born today, a hundred years will pass over it, and on that day it will not be alive."""
"5796","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no day on which Allah Almighty frees more people from the Fire than the Day of Arafah. On that day He draws near, then He boasts of them before the angels, saying: 'What do these people want?'"""
"5797","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""On every day on which the servants wake up in the morning, two angels descend. One of them says: 'O Allah, give the one who spends a replacement,' and the other says: 'O Allah, bring ruin to the wealth of the one who withholds.'"""
"5798","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is none among you except that Allah Almighty will speak to him on the Day of Resurrection, with no interpreter between him and Allah. He will look to his right and see nothing but what he sent forth, and he will look to his left and see nothing but what he sent forth, and he will look in front of him and see nothing but the Fire before his face. So protect yourselves from the Fire, even if by means of half a date, and even if by means of a good word."""
"5799","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Each one of you has two dwelling places: one in Paradise and one in Hell. So when he dies and enters Hell, the people of Paradise inherit his dwelling place in Paradise. This is the meaning of the saying of Allah Almighty: 'It is they who are the inheritors.'"""
"5800","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Each one of you has been assigned a companion from among the jinn and a companion from among the angels."" The Companions said: ""And you as well?"" He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Me as well, but Allah helped me against him, so he submitted, and now he commands me only to do good."""
"5801","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Each one of you has a devil attached to him."" The Companions said: ""And you as well, O Messenger of Allah?"" He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Me as well, but Allah helped me against him, so he submitted."""
"5802","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever among you performs ablution (wudu) and does it well, then stands and prays two rak'ahs, turning to them fully with his heart and his face, Paradise becomes obligatory for him and he is forgiven."""
"5803","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever among you performs ablution (wudu) and completes it thoroughly, then, on finishing his ablution, says: 'Ashhadu an la ilaha illallahu wahdahu la sharika lahu wa anna Muhammadan abduhu wa rasuluhu' (I bear witness that there is no true god except Allah, alone, without any partner, and that Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) is His servant and Messenger), the eight gates of Paradise are opened for him, and he may enter through whichever gate he wishes."""
"5804","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever among you draws near to his ablution water, rinses his mouth and spits the water out, and draws water into his nose and blows it out, the sins of his face, his mouth and his nostrils flow away. Then when he washes his face as Allah has commanded him, the sins of his face flow away with the water from the edges of his beard. Then he washes his hands up to the elbows, and the sins of his hands flow away with the water from the tips of his fingers. Then he wipes his head as Allah has commanded him, and the sins of his head flow away with the water from the ends of his hair. Then he washes his feet up to the ankles as Allah has commanded him, and the sins of his feet flow away with the water from the tips of his toes. Then if he stands and prays, and praises and extols Allah, and glorifies Him as He deserves, and empties his heart for Allah, he comes out purified of his sins just as he was on the day his mother gave birth to him."""
"5805","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Any woman among you whose three children die, they become a screen for her from Hell."" A woman said: ""And two?"" He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""And two as well suffice."""
"5806","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Ubayy, what prevented you from answering my call when I called you? Did you not find in what Allah has revealed to me: 'Respond to Allah and to the Messenger when he calls you to that which gives you life'?"""
"5807","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The one who withholds zakah will be in Hell on the Day of Resurrection."""
"5808","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""No wealth has ever benefited me as much as the wealth of Abu Bakr has benefited me."""
"5809","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Charity does not decrease wealth, and Allah increases a servant only in honour because of his forgiving, and whoever humbles himself for the sake of Allah, Allah raises him."""
"5810","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whatever I forbid you, avoid it, and whatever I command you, do as much of it as you are able, for those before you were destroyed only by their excessive questioning and their disagreeing with their prophets."""
"5811","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O owner of the grain, what is this? Why did you not put it on top of the grain so that people could see it? Whoever deceives is not of me."""
"5812","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Does the one who raises his head in prayer before the imam feel safe from Allah changing his form into the form of a donkey?!"""
"5813","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The martyr feels no more of the pain of being killed than one of you feels from the sting of an ant."""
"5814","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whenever a man gives out anything in charity, he first has to free it from the jaws of seventy devils."""
"5815","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Trials keep coming upon the believing man and the believing woman in their own selves, their children and their wealth, until they meet Allah with no sin remaining upon them."""
"5816","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A man keeps begging from people until he will come on the Day of Resurrection with not even a piece of flesh on his face."""
"5817","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""It would not please me to have gold equal to the mountain of Uhud and for three days to pass over me while even one dinar of it remained with me, except a dinar that I keep aside for a debt of mine."""
"5818","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whatever fatigue, illness, worry, grief, harm or distress befalls a Muslim, even a thorn that pricks him, Allah forgives some of his sins because of it."""
"5819","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whatever good I have, I will never hold it back from you. Whoever seeks to refrain from asking, Allah keeps him from it; whoever seeks self-sufficiency, Allah makes him self-sufficient; and whoever strives to be patient, Allah grants him patience. And no one has been given a gift better and more vast than patience."""
"5820","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""What prevents you from listening to what I advise you? That when you reach the morning and when you reach the evening you say: 'O Ever-Living, O Sustainer of all! By Your mercy I seek help. Set right all my affairs for me, and do not leave me to myself even for the blink of an eye.'"""
"5821","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""It is not fitting for any prophet to say: 'I am better than Yunus bin Matta.'"""
"5822","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Ibn Jamil has no excuse for not giving zakah except that he was poor and Allah made him rich. As for Khalid, you are wronging Khalid, for he has dedicated his armour and his war equipment in the path of Allah. As for Abbas, his zakah is upon me, and the same amount again. O Umar, do you not know that a man's paternal uncle is like his father?"""
"5823","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Give her the mut'ah (parting gift), for giving the mut'ah is necessary, even if it is only half a sa' of dates."""
"5824","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Give her the mut'ah, even if it is only a sa'."""
"5825","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The example of the son of Adam is that beside him are ninety-nine causes of death; if these causes miss him, he falls prey to old age and dies."""
"5826","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The example of the miser and the one who gives charity is that of two men wearing coats of iron armour from their chests to their collarbones. Whenever the spender spends anything, the armour expands over his body until it covers his fingertips and erases his footprints. And whenever the miser wants to spend anything, every ring of the armour sticks in its place; he tries to widen it, but it does not widen."""
"5827","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The example of the house in which Allah is remembered and the house in which Allah is not remembered is like that of the living and the dead."""
"5828","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The example of a righteous companion is like that of a perfume seller: even if he does not give you any of his perfume, its fragrance will surely reach you."""
"5829","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The example of a righteous companion and an evil companion is like that of a musk seller and a blacksmith's furnace. From the musk seller you will surely get something: either you will buy it, or at least its fragrance will reach you. As for the blacksmith's furnace, it will either burn your house or your clothes, or a foul smell from it will surely reach you."""
"5830","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The example of the five prayers is like a sweet, flowing river at the door of one of you, in which he bathes five times every day. Would any dirt remain on his body?"""
"5831","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The example of the scholar who teaches people good but forgets himself is like a lamp that gives light to people but burns itself."""
"5832","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The example of the one who upholds the limits of Allah and the one who is negligent concerning them is like that of people who cast lots for a ship at sea. Some of them got the upper part of the ship and some got the lower part. When those in the lower part wanted to get water, they would pass by those above them. So those in the upper part said: 'We will not let you come up and trouble us.' Those in the lower part said: 'What if we make a hole in our own part and do not trouble those above us?' So if those above leave them to what they intend, they will all perish, and if they hold them by their hands, they will be saved and all will be saved."""
"5833","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The example of the heart is like a feather that the winds turn over and over in an open wilderness."""
"5834","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The example of the one who gives charity and then takes it back is like a dog that vomits, then returns to its vomit and eats it."""
"5835","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The example of the one who learns knowledge and then does not pass it on is like one who amasses treasure and does not spend from it."""
"5836","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The example of the one who takes back what he gifted is like a dog that vomits and then eats its vomit. So if the giver wants to take back what he gave, he should be stopped and told on what basis he is taking it back, then what he gave should be handed over to him."""
"5837","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The example of the one who teaches people good but forgets himself is like a wick that gives light to people but burns itself."""
"5838","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The example of the one who helps his people in what is not right is like a camel that has fallen into a pit and is being pulled out by its tail."""
"5839","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The example of the believer who recites the Qur'an is like a citron (sweet lemon): its fragrance is good and its taste is good. The example of the believer who does not recite the Qur'an is like a date: its taste is good but it has no fragrance. The example of the wicked person who recites the Qur'an is like basil (a fragrant plant): its fragrance is good but its taste is bitter. The example of the wicked person who does not recite the Qur'an is like colocynth (bitter apple): its taste is bitter and it has no fragrance. The example of a righteous companion is like a musk seller: even if you get nothing from him, his fragrance will surely reach you. And the example of an evil companion is like the owner of a furnace: even if its soot does not touch you, its smoke will surely reach you."""
"5840","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The example of the believer who recites the Qur'an is like a citron: its fragrance is good and its taste is good. The example of the believer who does not recite the Qur'an is like a date: it has no fragrance but its taste is sweet. The example of the hypocrite who recites the Qur'an is like basil: its fragrance is good but its taste is bitter. And the example of the hypocrite who does not recite the Qur'an is like colocynth: it has no fragrance and its taste is not good."""
"5841","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The example of the believer is like a tender stalk of crops: the wind sometimes bends it and sometimes straightens it. And the example of the hypocrite is like a cedar tree that stands upright until it is uprooted all at once."""
"5842","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The example of the believer is like crops that the wind keeps bending, and trials keep befalling the believer as well. And the example of the hypocrite is like a cedar tree that does not sway until it is uprooted all at once."""
"5843","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The example of the believer is like a tender stalk of crops: from whichever direction the wind comes to it, it bends it, and when the wind subsides it stands straight again. Likewise the believer is bent by trials. And the example of the wicked person is like a sturdy, upright cedar tree, until Allah Almighty breaks it whenever He wills."""
"5844","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The example of the believer is like an ear of grain, which sometimes stands upright and sometimes bends down; and the example of the disbeliever is like the cedar tree, which remains standing upright until it suddenly falls without any warning."""
"5845","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The example of the believer is like an ear of grain, which sometimes bends and sometimes stands upright."""
"5846","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The example of the believer is like the honeybee: if it eats, it eats what is pure; if it deposits something, it deposits what is pure; and if it lands on a frail twig, it does not break it. And the example of the believer is also like an ingot of gold: if it is blown upon (in the fire), it turns red, and if it is weighed, it does not fall short."""
"5847","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The example of the believer is like the honeybee: it eats only what is pure and deposits only what is pure."""
"5848","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The example of the believer is like the date palm: whatever you take from it benefits you."""
"5849","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The example of the believers in their mutual love, mercy and compassion is like one body: when any limb of it suffers, the rest of the body joins it in sleeplessness and fever."""
"5850","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The example of the one who strives (does jihad) in the path of Allah - and Allah knows best who strives in His path - is like the one who fasts, stands in prayer, is humble, and bows and prostrates."""
"5851","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The example of the one who strives (does jihad) in the path of Allah - and Allah knows best who strives in His path - is like the one who continually fasts and stands in prayer, who does not tire of fasting and charity until he returns. And Allah Almighty has guaranteed for the one who strives in His path that if He causes him to die, He will admit him into Paradise, or else He will return him safe and sound with reward or spoils of war."""
"5852","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The example of the Muslims, the Jews and the Christians is like a man who hired some people to work for him until night. They worked until midday, then said: 'We have no need of the wage you fixed for us, nor of the work we have done for you.' He said to them: 'Do not do this; complete the rest of your work and take your full wage.' But they refused and abandoned it. Then after them he hired other labourers and said: 'Work the rest of your day, and you will have the wage I fixed for the first ones.' They worked until, when the time of the Asr prayer came, they said: 'What we have done is yours, and the wage you fixed for us is yours as well.' He said: 'Complete the rest of your work, for only a small part of the day remains.' But they refused. Then he hired some other people to work for him for the rest of the day. They worked the remainder of the day until the sun set, and they received in full the wages of both earlier groups. So this is their example, and the example of this light which they accepted."""
"5853","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The example of the hypocrite is like a stray sheep between two flocks: sometimes it runs towards this flock and sometimes towards that one, not knowing which of them to follow."""
"5854","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The example of my Ummah is like rain: it is not known whether its beginning is better or its end."""
"5855","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The example of the guidance and knowledge with which Allah has sent me is like abundant rain that falls on land. Part of it is fertile, absorbing the water and producing herbage and grass in abundance. Part of it is hard ground that holds the water, and Allah benefits people through it: they drink from it, give their animals to drink, and graze their livestock. And another part of it is barren plain that neither holds water nor grows any vegetation. That is the example of the one who gains understanding of the religion of Allah and benefits from what Allah has sent me with, so he learns and teaches others; and the example of the one who does not even raise his head towards it and does not accept the guidance with which I have been sent."""
"5856","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If something equal to the back post of a camel saddle is in front of any of you, then whoever passes in front of him does not harm him."""
"5857","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""My example among the prophets is like a man who built a house, made it excellent, complete and beautiful, but left the place of one brick empty in it. People began walking around the building, marvelling at it and saying: 'If only the place of this brick had been filled too!' So among the prophets, I am the place of that brick."""
"5858","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""My example is like a man who kindled a fire. When it lit up what was around him, moths and these insects that fall into fire began falling into it. He began holding them back, but they overpowered him and plunged into it. That is my example and yours: I am holding you back from the Fire: 'Keep away from the Fire, keep away from the Fire!' But you overpower me and plunge into it."""
"5859","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The example of me and you is like a man who kindled a fire, and moths and grasshoppers began falling into it while he kept driving them away from it. And I am holding you back from the Fire, but you slip out of my hand."""
"5860","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The example of me and of what Allah has sent me with is like a man who came to his people and said: 'O my people, I have seen the army with my own eyes, and I am a plain warner, so flee, flee!' A group of his people obeyed him; they set out by night, leaving at their ease, and were saved. Another group denied him and stayed where they were; the army attacked them in the morning and destroyed and annihilated them. That is the example of the one who obeys me and follows what I have brought, and of the one who disobeys me and denies the truth I have brought."""
"5861","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The one addicted to wine is like an idol worshipper."""
"5862","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Tell your sister to ride, for Allah Almighty has no need of your sister tormenting herself."""
"5863","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A man passed by the branch of a tree in the middle of a road and said: 'By Allah, I will remove this from the path of the Muslims so that it does not harm them.' So because of this good deed he was admitted into Paradise."""
"5864","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""On the night I was taken on the Night Journey (Mi'raj), I passed by the Highest Assembly (the exalted gathering of angels), and Jibril was shrunken like a worn-out old cloth out of fear of Allah Almighty."""
"5865","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""On the night I was taken on the Night Journey (Mi'raj), I passed by Musa (peace be upon him); he was standing in his grave, praying."""
"5866","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Tell Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer."""
"5867","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Command the child to pray when he reaches seven years of age, and when he reaches ten years, beat him for not praying."""
"5868","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Command your children to pray when they are seven years old, and beat them for it when they are ten years old, and separate their beds from one another."""
"5869","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Tell him to speak, to sit in the shade, to sit down, and to complete his fast."""
"5870","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Instruct her; if there is good in her, she will do it. And do not beat your wife the way you beat your slave woman."""
"5871","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A wealthy person's begging from people will be a blemish on his face on the Day of Resurrection."""
"5872","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""One who finds rest and one from whom rest is found: these are two kinds of people. The believing servant finds rest from the toil and hardship of this world and goes on to the mercy of Allah Almighty; and with the death of the wicked servant, people, lands, trees and animals all find rest."""
"5873","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The matter of Hijrah has passed for its people. I take his pledge of allegiance on Islam and jihad."""
"5874","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Rinse your mouths after drinking milk, for it contains fat."""
"5875","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A wealthy person's delaying the repayment of a debt is injustice. So when any of you is referred (for payment) to a wealthy person, let him accept it."""
"5876","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A wealthy person's delaying is injustice, and when you are referred to a wealthy person, follow it."""
"5877","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""With the boy there is an Aqiqah due, so shed blood on his behalf and remove the harm from him."""
"5878","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I seek refuge in Allah from people saying that I kill my companions! Indeed, this man and his companions recite the Qur'an, but it does not go beyond their throats. They will pass out of the religion just as an arrow passes through the game."""
"5879","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Mu'adh bin Jabal is the most knowledgeable of people regarding what is lawful and unlawful."""
"5880","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""On the Day of Resurrection, Mu'adh bin Jabal will be ahead of the scholars by the distance of an arrow's shot."""
"5881","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The real battlefield where death strikes is between the ages of sixty and seventy."""
"5882","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There are some phrases repeated after every obligatory prayer whose sayer never fails: Subhan Allah 33 times, al-Hamdu lillah 33 times, and Allahu Akbar 34 times."""
"5883","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Everything seeks forgiveness for the one who teaches good, even the fish in the sea."""
"5884","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The keys of the Unseen are five, which no one knows except Allah Almighty: no one knows what will happen tomorrow except Allah Almighty; no one knows what is in the wombs of mothers except Allah Almighty; no one knows when the Hour will be established except Allah Almighty; no soul knows in which land it will die except Allah Almighty; and no one knows when the rain will come except Allah Almighty."""
"5885","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The key to prayer is purification; it begins with the Takbir and it ends with the Salam."""
"5886","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A man's standing in the rank in the path of Allah is better than sixty years of worship."""
"5887","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""May Allah fill their houses and their graves with fire, just as they kept us occupied from the middle prayer until the sun set."""
"5888","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Ammar has been filled with faith down to the joints of his bones."""
"5889","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Cursed is the one who approaches a woman through her anus."""
"5890","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Cursed is the one who asks by the Face of Allah, and cursed is the one who is asked by the Face of Allah and then refuses the one asking, as long as the one asking does not ask for something improper."""
"5891","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Cursed is the one who reviles his father; cursed is the one who reviles his mother; cursed is the one who slaughters for other than Allah; cursed is the one who alters the boundary markers of the land; cursed is the one who misleads a blind person from the road; cursed is the one who has intercourse with an animal; cursed is the one who does the deed of the people of Lut."""
"5892","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Among the people who will receive the severest punishment on the Day of Resurrection are those who make these images."""
"5893","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Among those of my Ummah who love me most intensely are people who will come after me; each one of them will wish that he could see me in exchange for his family and his wealth."""
"5894","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Among the signs of the Hour are that obscenity and the spread of obscenity will occur, ties of kinship will be severed, the trustworthy will be regarded as treacherous, and the treacherous will be regarded as trustworthy."""
"5895","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Among the signs of the Hour is also that people will boast to one another over the building and adornment of mosques."""
"5896","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Among the signs of the Hour is also that a man passes through a mosque and does not pray two rak'ahs in it, and that a man greets with salam only those whom he knows."""
"5897","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Among the most excellent of deeds is bringing happiness to a believer: paying off his debt, fulfilling some need of his, or relieving some hardship of his."""
"5898","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Among the signs of the Hour drawing near is also that the crescent moons will appear large."""
"5899","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Among the signs of the Hour drawing near is also that the crescent will be seen on the very first day, and it will be said that it is the moon of two nights; that mosques will be taken as thoroughfares; and that sudden death will become widespread."""
"5900","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Among the greatest of the major sins are associating partners with Allah and swearing a false oath."""
"5901","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""It is also part of righteousness that you maintain ties with your father's friend."""
"5902","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Wine is also made from dates and half-ripe dates."""
"5903","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Wine is made from wheat, wine is made from dates, wine is made from barley, wine is made from raisins, and wine is made from honey."""
"5904","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Among the prayers is a prayer which, if someone misses it, it is as though his family and his wealth were snatched away from him (that is, the Asr prayer)."""
"5905","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Among jealousy there is some that Allah loves and some that Allah dislikes. The jealousy that Allah loves is jealousy where there is suspicion, and the jealousy that Allah dislikes is jealousy without any suspicion."""
"5906","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The following are part of the fitrah: rinsing the mouth, drawing water into the nose, using the miswak, trimming the moustache, clipping the nails, plucking the armpit hair, shaving the pubic hair, washing the finger joints, sprinkling water after istinja, and circumcision."""
"5907","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The following are part of the fitrah: shaving the pubic hair, clipping the nails and trimming the moustache."""
"5908","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Among the major sins is also that a man reviles his own parents, in that he reviles another man's father and so that man reviles his father, and he reviles someone's mother and so that person reviles his mother."""
"5909","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""This is from Allah Almighty, not from His Messenger: Allah has cursed the one who cuts down the lote tree."""
"5910","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The discharge of madhi requires ablution (wudu), and the discharge of mani requires a ritual bath (ghusl)."""
"5911","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Part of the excellence of a person's Islam is that he leaves alone what does not concern him."""
"5912","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you goes out from his house to the mosque, one of his steps records a good deed and the other step erases a sin."""
"5913","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Among your caliphs there will be a caliph who will give out wealth freely in handfuls, and will not count it out."""
"5914","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best of your perfumes is musk."""
"5915","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Among the best ways of life for people is a man who holds the reins of his horse in the path of Allah, flying about on its back; whenever he hears a cry of danger or alarm, he flies towards it, seeking out the places of martyrdom and death. And the other is a man who lives with his goats on the summit of one of these mountain peaks, or in the bottom of one of these valleys, establishing the prayer, giving zakah and worshipping his Lord until death comes to him; such a person remains among people only in goodness."""
"5916","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Among the worst of people are also those whom the Hour overtakes while they are still alive."""
"5917","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Among the worst of people is also the two-faced person, who comes to these people with one face and to those people with another face."""
"5918","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever washes him (the deceased) must take a ritual bath (ghusl), and whoever carries him must perform ablution (wudu)."""
"5919","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Trials will come from here"" - and he (peace and blessings be upon him) pointed towards the east - ""and harshness and hardness of heart are among those loud-voiced herdsmen, the tent-dwelling people who work near the roots of the tails of camels and cattle, that is, among the tribes of Rabi'ah and Mudar."""
"5920","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""From among us will be the one behind whom Isa bin Maryam will pray."""
"5921","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever is given something of this wealth by Allah without his having asked for it, let him accept it, for it is only provision that Allah has sent to him."""
"5922","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever hurts Abbas has hurt me; indeed, a man's paternal uncle is the equal of his father."""
"5923","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever harms the Muslims on their roads, their curse becomes binding upon him."""
"5924","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever hurts Ali has hurt me."""
"5925","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever believes in Allah and His Messenger, establishes the prayer, gives zakah and fasts in Ramadan, it becomes a right upon Allah that He admits him into Paradise, whether he migrated in the path of Allah or stayed in the very land in which he was born."""
"5926","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever keeps a stray animal with him without announcing it is himself astray, so long as he does not announce it."""
"5927","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever buys foodstuff, let him not sell it on until he has taken full possession of it."""
"5928","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever buys an animal whose udder has been tied to show more milk has the option for three days: if he wishes, he may keep it, and if he wishes, he may return it, and along with it he should give a sa' of dates, not wheat."""
"5929","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever buys a date palm after it has been pollinated, its fruit belongs to the seller unless the buyer stipulates otherwise; and whoever buys a slave who has wealth, his wealth belongs to the one who sold him unless the buyer stipulates otherwise."""
"5930","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever seeks knowledge in order to boast with it before the scholars, or to argue and dispute with it against the foolish, or to turn people's hearts towards himself, his end is the Fire."""
"5931","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever is tested with daughters and is patient with them, they become a screen for him from the Fire."""
"5932","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever is tested with these daughters and treats them well, they become a screen for him from the Fire."""
"5933","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever is shown a favour and mentions it has thanked for it, and if he conceals it, he has been ungrateful for it."""
"5934","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever goes to visit his sick Muslim brother walks among the fruits of Paradise until he sits down, and when he sits down, mercy covers him. If it is morning, seventy thousand angels pray for mercy for him until the evening, and if it is evening, seventy thousand angels pray for him until the morning."""
"5935","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever comes to the Friday prayer, let him take a ritual bath (ghusl)."""
"5936","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever comes to the mosque for something, that is his share."""
"5937","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever does you a kindness, repay him, and if you find no means of repaying him, then supplicate for him."""
"5938","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever commits bestiality with an animal, kill him, and kill the animal along with him."""
"5939","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever goes to a fortune-teller or a soothsayer and believes what he says has disbelieved in what was revealed to Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him)."""
"5940","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever goes to a fortune-teller and asks him about something, his prayer will not be accepted for forty nights."""
"5941","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever goes to his bed intending to get up at night and pray, but sleep overcomes him until morning comes, the reward is recorded for him according to his intention, and his sleep is a charity to him from his Lord."""
"5942","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever goes to a soothsayer and believes what he says, or goes to a woman during her menstruation, or goes to a woman through her anus, has disassociated himself from what was revealed to Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him)."""
"5943","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever performs Hajj to this House (the Ka'bah) and neither speaks indecently nor commits sin returns like the day his mother gave birth to him."""
"5944","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever comes to you while your affair is united under one man, wanting to break your unity and divide your community, then kill him."""
"5945","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever reaches sixty years of age, Allah Almighty has left him no excuse in the matter of his lifespan."""
"5946","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever keeps a dog other than a dog for farming or hunting, one qirat is deducted from his reward every day."""
"5947","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever performs ablution completely, just as Allah has commanded him, then the obligatory prayers become an expiation for the sins between them."""
"5948","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever is attacked for the sake of his wealth, and fights and is killed, he is a martyr."""
"5949","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever loses three of his own children in the path of Allah and seeks their reward from Allah, Paradise becomes obligatory for him."""
"5950","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever you speak well of, Paradise becomes obligatory for him, and whoever you speak ill of, Hell becomes obligatory for him. You are the witnesses of Allah on earth."""
"5951","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever honours the authority appointed by Allah, Allah will honour him on the Day of Resurrection."""
"5952","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever builds a wall around a piece of land, that land becomes his."""
"5953","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever loves the Ansar, Allah loves him, and whoever hates the Ansar, Allah hates him."""
"5954","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever loves Hasan and Husayn has loved me, and whoever hates them has hated me."""
"5955","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever wishes that his record of deeds should please him, let him seek forgiveness (istighfar) abundantly in it."""
"5956","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever wishes that his provision be expanded and his lifespan be extended, let him maintain the ties of kinship."""
"5957","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever loves that people should stand up before him, let him take his seat in Hell."""
"5958","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever wishes to taste the sweetness of faith, let him love a person solely for the sake of Allah."""
"5959","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever wishes to ask about something, let him ask. By Allah, whatever you ask me about, I will tell you about it as long as I remain in this place of mine. By the One in whose hand is my soul, just now, while I was praying, Paradise and Hell were presented to me in front of this wall. I have never seen anything like today in good and evil."""
"5960","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever wishes to maintain ties with his father even in his grave, let him maintain ties with his father's brothers (friends) after him."""
"5961","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever wishes to recite the Qur'an fresh, just as it was revealed, let him recite according to the recitation of Ibn Umm Abd."""
"5962","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever wishes to see what a martyr walking on the earth looks like, let him look at Talhah bin Abdullah."""
"5963","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever loves Ali has loved me, and whoever hates Ali has hated me."""
"5964","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever loves meeting Allah, Allah also loves meeting him, and whoever dislikes meeting Allah, Allah also dislikes meeting him."""
"5965","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever loves for the sake of Allah, hates for the sake of Allah, gives for the sake of Allah and withholds for the sake of Allah has perfected his faith."""
"5966","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever loves me, let him also love Usamah."""
"5967","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever keeps a horse in the path of Allah out of faith in Allah and affirmation of His promise, then its food, its drink, its dung and its urine will all come as good deeds in his scale on the Day of Resurrection."""
"5968","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever has cupping done on the seventeenth, nineteenth or twenty-first of the month, it will be a cure for him from every disease."""
"5969","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever seeks reward from Allah for the death of three of his children will enter Paradise."" A woman said: ""And two?"" He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""And two as well suffice."""
"5970","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever introduces into this religion of ours something new that is not part of it, it is rejected."""
"5971","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever enters ihram for both Hajj and Umrah, one tawaf and one sa'y suffice him for both, and he will not leave ihram until he completes his Hajj; then he will leave ihram from both together."""
"5972","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever becomes skilled in archery and then abandons it has abandoned a blessing."""
"5973","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever does good deeds after accepting Islam will not be held to account for his deeds in the Days of Ignorance (Jahiliyyah), and whoever does evil after accepting Islam will be held to account for both the earlier and the later."""
"5974","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever revives barren land will have a reward for it, and whatever animals eat from it is charity for him."""
"5975","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever revives barren land, that land becomes his."""
"5976","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever revives barren land, that land becomes his, and a root planted unjustly has no right."""
"5977","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever terrifies the people of Madinah, Allah will terrify him."""
"5978","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever terrifies the people of Madinah has terrified my heart within my chest."""
"5979","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever recites the Qur'an according to a seventh portion, that is better."""
"5980","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever takes people's wealth intending to repay it, Allah will repay it on his behalf, and whoever takes it intending to squander it, Allah will destroy him."""
"5981","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever takes a loan while intending to repay it, Allah helps him."""
"5982","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever takes a bow in return for teaching the Qur'an, Allah will hang around his neck in its place a bow from the fire of Hell on the Day of Resurrection."""
"5983","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever wrongfully takes any part of a piece of land will be sunk into it down to seven earths on the Day of Resurrection."""
"5984","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever takes any part of a piece of land unjustly will come on the Day of Resurrection carrying its soil to the plain of gathering."""
"5985","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever removes something harmful from the path of the Muslims, Allah records one good deed for him because of it, and whoever has one good deed recorded for him with Allah, He will admit him to Paradise because of it."""
"5986","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever takes a loan with the intention of repaying it, Allah will repay that loan on his behalf on the Day of Resurrection."""
"5987","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever attributes himself to someone other than his father, or claims affiliation to someone other than his masters, upon him is the continuous curse of Allah until the Day of Resurrection."""
"5988","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever attributes himself to someone other than his father will not even find the fragrance of Paradise, although its fragrance can be perceived from a distance of five hundred years."""
"5989","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever knowingly attributes himself to someone other than his father, Paradise is forbidden to him."""
"5990","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever claims something that is not his is not one of us, and let him take his seat in Hell."""
"5991","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever catches one rak'ah of the Friday prayer, let him add another rak'ah to it."""
"5992","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever catches one rak'ah of the Fajr prayer before the sun rises has caught Fajr, and whoever catches one rak'ah of the Asr prayer before the sun sets has caught Asr."""
"5993","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever catches one rak'ah of the prayer with the imam has caught that prayer."""
"5994","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever catches one rak'ah of the Friday prayer or of any other prayer, his prayer is complete."""
"5995","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever reaches Arafah before the break of dawn has caught the Hajj."""
"5996","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever finds his own property exactly as it was with a man who has become bankrupt, he has more right to that property than anyone else."""
"5997","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever catches this prayer with us, that is, the Fajr prayer, having already come to Arafat before that, by night or by day, has completed his rites and his Hajj is complete."""
"5998","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever catches one rak'ah of the prayer has caught that prayer."""
"5999","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever catches one rak'ah of the Friday prayer has caught that prayer."""
"6000","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever catches one rak'ah of a prayer has caught that prayer."""
"6001","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever among you meets Isa bin Maryam, let him convey my greeting of peace to him."""
"6002","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever gives the call to prayer (adhan) for twelve years, Paradise becomes obligatory for him, and for his daily adhan sixty good deeds are recorded for him, and for his iqamah thirty good deeds."""
"6003","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever intends to perform Hajj, let him hasten."""
"6004","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever intends to perform Hajj, let him hasten, for a person may fall ill, something may go missing, and some need may arise."""
"6005","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever intends to fast, let him eat something at the pre-dawn meal (suhur)."""
"6006","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever wishes to know what standing he has with Allah, let him look at what standing Allah has with him."""
"6007","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever intends evil against the people of Madinah, Allah will dissolve him just as salt dissolves in water."""
"6008","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever keeps a horse tethered in the path of Allah and then prepares its fodder with his own hand, he receives one good deed for every grain."""
"6009","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever turns away from his religion, kill him."""
"6010","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever pleases people by angering Allah, Allah entrusts him to the people themselves; and whoever angers people by pleasing Allah, Allah protects him from the harm of people."""
"6011","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever's wealth is sought to be taken unjustly, and he fights in its defence and is killed, he is a martyr."""
"6012","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever lets his lower garment hang down in his prayer out of arrogance, there is no matter of lawful or unlawful for him with Allah."""
"6013","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever cleans himself with stones after relieving himself, let him use three (an odd number)."""
"6014","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever establishes a good practice and it is acted upon, he will have its full reward, and he will also have the reward of those who act upon it, without anything being reduced from their reward; and whoever establishes an evil practice and it is acted upon, he will bear its full sin, and he will also bear the sin of those who act upon it, without anything being reduced from their sin."""
"6015","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever is able to die in Madinah, let him die there, for I will intercede for whoever dies there."""
"6016","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever among you is able to ensure that nothing comes between him and his qiblah, let him do so."""
"6017","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever among you is able to shield himself from the Fire, even with a piece of a date, let him do so."""
"6018","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever among you is able to have a hidden righteous deed, let him do so."""
"6019","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever among you is able to benefit his brother, let him benefit him."""
"6020","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever seeks refuge by invoking Allah, grant him refuge; and whoever asks of you for the sake of Allah, give to him."""
"6021","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever seeks refuge with you by invoking Allah, grant him refuge; whoever asks of you by invoking Allah, give to him; whoever invites you, accept his invitation; and whoever does you a kindness, repay him; and if you find nothing with which to repay him, then pray for him until you are sure that you have repaid him."""
"6022","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever seeks to refrain from asking, Allah keeps him from it; whoever seeks self-sufficiency, Allah makes him self-sufficient; and whoever asks people while he has the equivalent of five uqiyah has asked with unjustified insistence."""
"6023","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whomever we appoint to a post and provide with a stipend, whatever he takes beyond that is misappropriation."""
"6024","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whomever among you we appoint to a post and he conceals from us a needle or anything greater, that is misappropriation which he will bring with him on the Day of Resurrection."""
"6025","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whomever among you we appoint to a post, let him bring everything of it, little and much; then whatever he is given of it he may take, and whatever he is forbidden he should refrain from."""
"6026","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever seeks forgiveness for the believing men and believing women, Allah records for him a good deed for every believing man and believing woman."""
"6027","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever seeks self-sufficiency, Allah makes him self-sufficient; whoever seeks to refrain from asking, Allah keeps him from it; whoever seeks sufficiency, Allah suffices him; and whoever asks while he possesses the equivalent of one uqiyah has asked with insistence."""
"6028","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever listens to the conversation of people while they dislike his listening, molten lead will be poured into his ears; and whoever falsely claims to have seen with his eyes in a dream what he did not see will be made to tie a knot in a grain of barley."""
"6029","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever is entrusted with a deposit, there is no liability upon him."""
"6030","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever wakes up at night and also wakes his wife, and then they both pray two rak'ahs together, they are recorded that night among the men and women who remember Allah much."""
"6031","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever makes an advance payment (salaf) for something, let him do so for a known measure, a known weight and a known term."""
"6032","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever accepts Islam while owning something, that thing remains his."""
"6033","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever accepts Islam at the hands of a man, his wala' (patronage) belongs to that man."""
"6034","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever points a weapon at his brother, the angels curse him, even if he is his full brother."""
"6035","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever buys a sheep whose udder has been tied to make its milk appear more has the option for three days; if he returns it, he should give a sa' of foodstuff along with it, not wheat."""
"6036","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever buys a sheep whose udder has been tied has the better of two options: if he wishes, he may keep it, and if he wishes, he may return it along with a sa' of dates, not wheat."""
"6037","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever buys a sheep whose udder has been tied has the option for three days: if he wishes, he may keep it, and if he wishes, he may return it along with a sa' of dates."""
"6038","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever out of need eats something with his mouth and does not carry any away hidden, there is nothing upon him; whoever carries some of it away with him owes a fine of twice its value and a punishment; whoever steals some of it after it has reached the drying place for fruit, and it reaches the value of a shield, his hand is to be cut off; and whoever steals less than that owes a fine of twice its value and a punishment."""
"6039","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever commits a sin and the prescribed punishment (hadd) for that sin is carried out on him, that is its expiation."""
"6040","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever is afflicted by worry, grief, illness or hardship and says: 'Allah is my Lord, He has no partner,' it is removed from him."""
"6041","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever is afflicted by poverty and presents it before people, his poverty is not ended; and whoever presents it before Allah, Allah soon grants him sufficiency, either through a death that comes later or through immediate wealth."""
"6042","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever among you begins the morning secure in his home, healthy in his body, and having the food for that day, it is as though the whole world has been gathered for him."""
"6043","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever lies down in a place and does not remember Allah in it, it will be a cause of regret for him on the Day of Resurrection; and whoever sits in a place and does not remember Allah in it, it too will be a cause of regret for him on the Day of Resurrection."""
"6044","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever obeys me has obeyed Allah, and whoever disobeys me has disobeyed Allah; whoever obeys the leader has obeyed me, and whoever disobeys the leader has disobeyed me."""
"6045","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever Allah gives some food to eat, let him say: 'O Allah, bless it for us and feed us with something better than it.' And whoever Allah gives milk to drink, let him say: 'O Allah, bless it for us and give us more of it.' For there is nothing other than milk that suffices as both food and drink."""
"6046","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever peeps into someone's house without permission, and they then gouge out his eye, there is neither blood money nor retaliation for him."""
"6047","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever peeps into someone's house without their permission, it becomes lawful for them to gouge out his eye."""
"6048","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever peeps into someone's house without their permission, and they then gouge out his eye, it is forfeited (with no compensation)."""
"6049","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever helps in a dispute unjustly remains under the displeasure of Allah until he desists."""
"6050","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever frees a believing slave, it becomes his ransom from Hell."""
"6051","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever frees a Muslim slave, Allah frees, in return for every limb of the slave, one limb of the one who freed him from Hell, even his private part in return for the slave's private part."""
"6052","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever frees his share in a jointly owned slave, and he has enough wealth to cover the full price of the slave, the slave will be given a fair valuation, he will pay his partners their shares, and the slave will be completely free; otherwise only as much of him is freed as he freed."""
"6053","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever frees part of a slave, it is binding on him to secure the slave's complete freedom from his own wealth. If he has no wealth, the slave will be given a fair valuation, and then he will be given the opportunity to earn the price of the remaining share without being overburdened."""
"6054","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever frees a slave who has wealth, that wealth remains the slave's, unless the master stipulates that wealth for himself, in which case it will be the master's."""
"6055","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever is given his share of gentleness has been given his share of goodness, and whoever is deprived of his share of gentleness has been deprived of his share of goodness."""
"6056","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever is given something and has the means, let him repay it; and if he does not have the means, let him praise the giver. Whoever praises him has thanked him, and whoever conceals it has been ungrateful. And whoever adorns himself with something he has not been given is like one who wears two garments of falsehood."""
"6057","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever cultivates land that belongs to no one has the greater right to it."""
"6058","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever gives a man something as an umra (a lifetime gift), it becomes his and his descendants'; whichever of his descendants is his heir will inherit it."""
"6059","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever gives something as an umra (a lifetime gift), it becomes the recipient's, both in his lifetime and after his death. And do not make ruqba (a gift conditional on survival), for whoever gives something as a ruqba, it follows the course of inheritance."""
"6060","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever is given something as an umra (a lifetime gift), it becomes his, both in his lifetime and after his death."""
"6061","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever's feet become dusty in the path of Allah, Allah makes him forbidden to the Fire."""
"6062","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever performs the ritual bath (ghusl) on Friday, then comes to the Friday prayer and prays whatever has been decreed for him, then remains silent until the imam finishes his sermon, then prays with him, his sins between that and the next Friday are forgiven, and three more days in addition."""
"6063","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever performs a ritual bath on Friday like the bath for major impurity (janabah) and then goes out in the first hour, it is as if he offered a camel in sacrifice; whoever goes out in the second hour, it is as if he offered a cow; whoever goes out in the third hour, it is as if he offered a horned ram; whoever goes out in the fourth hour, it is as if he offered a hen; and whoever goes out in the fifth hour, it is as if he offered an egg. Then when the imam comes out, the angels come in to listen to the remembrance."""
"6064","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever performs the ritual bath well on Friday, purifies himself well, puts on his best clothes, and applies whatever perfume or household oil Allah has decreed for him, then comes to the mosque and neither engages in idle talk nor separates two people, Allah forgives him his sins between that and the next Friday."""
"6065","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever performs the ritual bath (ghusl) on Friday remains in a state of purity until the next Friday."""
"6066","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever performs the ritual bath (ghusl) on Friday, uses the tooth-stick (miswak), applies perfume if he has any, puts on his best clothes, then goes out and comes to the mosque without stepping over people's necks, then offers as much voluntary prayer as he wishes, then keeps silent when the imam comes out and does not speak until his prayer is finished, it becomes an expiation for the sins between that Friday and the next."""
"6067","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever performs the ritual bath (ghusl) on Friday, applies some of his wife's perfume if she has any, puts on his good clothes, then does not step over people's necks and does not engage in idle talk during the sermon, it becomes an expiation for his sins; and whoever engages in idle talk and steps over people's necks, for him it will be merely equal to the Zuhr prayer."""
"6068","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever gives a fatwa without knowledge, its sin will be upon the one who gave the fatwa; and whoever advises his brother on a matter while knowing that the right course lies elsewhere has betrayed him."""
"6069","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever gives a fatwa without verification, its sin will be only upon the one who gave the fatwa."""
"6070","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever breaks his fast in Ramadan out of forgetfulness owes neither a make-up fast nor an expiation."""
"6071","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever cancels a transaction with a Muslim at his request, Allah Almighty will forgive his slip."""
"6072","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever presents proof of having captured a prisoner, the prisoner's belongings are his."""
"6073","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever settles among the polytheists, the protection of the Muslims is withdrawn from him."""
"6074","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever learns something of the knowledge of the stars has learned a branch of magic; the more he increases in it, the more it increases."""
"6075","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever seizes land unjustly will meet Allah while He is angry with him."""
"6076","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever seizes the right of a Muslim by his false oath, Allah has made Hell obligatory for him and Paradise forbidden to him, even if it is only a twig of the arak tree."""
"6077","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever keeps a dog other than a dog for livestock or for hunting, two qirats are deducted from his deeds every day."""
"6078","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever keeps a dog that is neither a hunting dog, nor a livestock dog, nor a farm dog, two qirats are deducted from his reward every day."""
"6079","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever keeps a dog that is of no use to him for crops or livestock, one qirat is deducted from his deeds every day."""
"6080","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever lends silver twice, it is equal to giving it in charity once."""
"6081","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever has himself cauterised or seeks ruqyah (incantation) has abandoned complete reliance on Allah."""
"6082","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever eats or drinks out of forgetfulness, his fast is not broken, for it is merely provision that Allah has given him."""
"6083","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever eats a meal unlawfully by means of a Muslim, Allah will feed him the like of it from Hell; whoever wears a garment by means of a Muslim, Allah will clothe him with the like of it from Hell; and whoever attains a position of fame and show by means of a Muslim, Allah will make him stand in a position of fame and show on the Day of Resurrection."""
"6084","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever eats garlic or onion, let him keep away from us, keep away from our mosque, and stay in his house."""
"6085","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever eats seven dates from what lies between the two lava fields of Madinah in the morning, no poison will harm him that day until evening."""
"6086","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever eats food and then says: 'Alhamdu lillahil-ladhi at'amani hadhat-ta'ama wa razaqanihi min ghayri hawlin minni wa la quwwah' (All praise is for Allah who fed me this food and provided it for me without any power or strength on my part), his past sins are forgiven. And whoever puts on a garment and says: 'Alhamdu lillahil-ladhi kasani hadha wa razaqanihi min ghayri hawlin minni wa la quwwah' (All praise is for Allah who clothed me with this and provided it for me without any power or strength on my part), all his past and future sins are forgiven."""
"6087","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever eats meat, let him perform ablution (wudu)."""
"6088","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever eats dates with a group of people, let him not eat two at a time, unless they give him permission."""
"6089","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever eats any of these vegetables, garlic, onion or leek, let him not come near us in our mosques, for the angels are also harmed by what harms the children of Adam."""
"6090","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever eats anything of this foul-smelling plant, let him not come near us in the mosque. O people, it is not for me to forbid what Allah has made lawful, but it is a plant whose smell I dislike."""
"6091","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever eats of this foul-smelling plant, let him not come near our mosque, for the angels are also harmed by what harms human beings."""
"6092","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever eats from this foul-smelling plant should not come near our place of prayer until its smell has gone."""
"6093","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever eats from this plant should not come near the mosques."""
"6094","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever eats from this plant should not come near our mosque, nor trouble us with the smell of garlic."""
"6095","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever eats from this plant should not come near us, nor pray with us."""
"6096","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever eats from this plant - meaning garlic - should not come near our mosque."""
"6097","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever seeks the pleasure of Allah even if people become displeased, Allah will suffice him against the burden of people; and whoever seeks the pleasure of people even if Allah becomes displeased, Allah will leave him to the people."""
"6098","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever removes something harmful from the path of the Muslims, a good deed is recorded for him; and whoever has a good deed accepted from him will enter Paradise."""
"6099","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever among the rulers commands you to commit a sin, do not obey him."""
"6100","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever keeps a dog, one qirat is deducted from his deeds every day, except for a dog for farming or a dog for livestock."""
"6101","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever leads people in prayer and performs the prayer at its proper time and completes it, the reward is for him and for them; and whoever falls short in any of that, the burden of it is upon him and not upon them."""
"6102","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever leads a people in prayer while they dislike him, his prayer does not rise above his collarbone."""
"6103","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever grants a man safety for his life and then kills him, I am free of the killer, even if the one killed was a disbeliever."""
"6104","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever attributes himself to someone other than his father, or takes as patrons others than his own masters, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels and all the people."""
"6105","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever engages in plunder is not one of us."""
"6106","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever grants respite to a debtor in hardship, or waives his debt, Allah will shade him in His shade on the day when there is no shade but His shade."""
"6107","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever grants respite to a debtor in hardship, or waives his debt, Allah will shade him on the Day of Resurrection beneath the shade of His Throne, on the day when there is no shade but His shade."""
"6108","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever grants respite to a debtor in hardship, then for every day before the debt falls due he receives the like of it as charity; and when the debt falls due and he still grants him respite, then for every day he receives twice as much as charity."""
"6109","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever spends a pair (two of something) in the way of Allah will be called from the gates of Paradise: 'O servant of Allah, this is good.' So whoever is among the people of prayer will be called from the gate of prayer; whoever is among the people of jihad will be called from the gate of jihad; whoever is among the people of fasting will be called from the gate of al-Rayyan; and whoever is among the people of charity will be called from the gate of charity. Abu Bakr said: 'Will anyone be called from all of those gates?' He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: 'Yes, and I hope that you will be among them.'"""
"6110","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever spends something in the way of Allah, it is recorded for him seven hundred times over."""
"6111","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever dishonours the authority of Allah on earth, Allah will dishonour him."""
"6112","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever dishonours Quraysh, Allah will dishonour him."""
"6113","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever spends the night on the roof of a house that has no protective wall, the protection of Allah is lifted from him."""
"6114","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever goes to sleep with the smell of grease on his hand and is then afflicted with a skin disease, let him blame no one but himself."""
"6115","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever goes to sleep with grease on his hand and is then afflicted with some harm, let him blame no one but himself."""
"6116","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever makes two sales in one sale, he is entitled to the lower price of the two, or else it is usury (riba)."""
"6117","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever sells fruit and it is then struck by a calamity should not take anything from his brother's wealth. On what basis would any of you consume the wealth of his Muslim brother?!"""
"6118","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever sells the hide of his sacrificial animal, his sacrifice does not count."""
"6119","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever sells a house and then does not put its price into something similar, it will not be blessed for him."""
"6120","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever among you sells a house or property, let him know that it is wealth that is very likely not to be blessed for him, unless he puts it into something similar."""
"6121","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever is first to give the greeting of salam is the closer to Allah and His Messenger."""
"6122","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever begins speaking before giving the greeting of salam, do not answer him."""
"6123","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever settles in the desert becomes harsh."""
"6124","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever settles in the desert becomes harsh; whoever keeps chasing game becomes heedless; and whoever keeps going to the doors of rulers falls into trial."""
"6125","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever changes his religion, kill him."""
"6126","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever shoots an arrow in the way of Allah and it reaches its target, it will be a rank for him in Paradise."""
"6127","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever builds a mosque for Allah, Allah builds for him a house in Paradise."""
"6128","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever builds a mosque for Allah, even if it is as small as a sandgrouse's nest or smaller, Allah builds for him a house in Paradise."""
"6129","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever builds a mosque for Allah, even if it is as small as the nest a sandgrouse makes for its eggs, Allah builds for him a house in Paradise."""
"6130","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever builds for Allah a mosque in which Allah is remembered, Allah builds for him the like of it in Paradise."""
"6131","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever builds a mosque seeking thereby the pleasure of Allah, Allah builds for him the like of it in Paradise."""
"6132","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever repents to Allah before the death rattle, Allah accepts his repentance."""
"6133","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever repents before the sun rises from the west, Allah accepts his repentance."""
"6134","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever follows a funeral until the prayer is offered over it receives one qirat of reward, and whoever walks with the funeral until it is buried receives two qirats of reward, and one qirat is equal to Mount Uhud."""
"6135","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever follows a funeral until the prayer is offered over it and it is finished with receives two qirats, and whoever follows it until the prayer is offered over it receives one qirat. By the One in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him), it will be heavier in his scale than Mount Uhud."""
"6136","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever follows a funeral until it is finished with receives two qirats, and if he returns before it is finished with, he receives one qirat."""
"6137","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever follows a funeral, prays over it and then leaves receives one qirat of reward; and whoever follows it, prays over it, then remains seated until it and its burial are finished receives two qirats of reward, each of which is greater than Mount Uhud."""
"6138","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever follows the funeral of a Muslim out of faith and seeking reward, and stays with it until the prayer is offered over it and the burial is finished, returns with two qirats of reward, each qirat being equal to Mount Uhud; and whoever prays over it and then returns before it is buried returns with one qirat of reward."""
"6139","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever fabricates a dream falsely will be charged on the Day of Resurrection with tying a knot between two grains of barley, and he will never be able to tie it."""
"6140","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever misses three Friday prayers in a row without necessity, Allah places a seal upon his heart."""
"6141","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever leaves snakes alone out of fear of their pursuit is not one of us. We have never made peace with them since we went to war with them."""
"6142","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever gives up archery after having learned it, out of disinclination for it, then it is a blessing for which he has been ungrateful."""
"6143","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever misses three Friday prayers out of negligence, Allah sets a seal upon his heart."""
"6144","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever misses three Friday prayers without an excuse is recorded among the hypocrites."""
"6145","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever gives up fine clothing out of humility for the sake of Allah, while he is able to afford it, Allah will call him on the Day of Resurrection before all of creation and give him the choice to wear whichever of the garments of faith he wishes."""
"6146","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever abandons the Asr prayer, his deeds are rendered void."""
"6147","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever leaves behind wealth, it belongs to his heirs; and whoever leaves behind a burden, it is the responsibility of Allah and His Messenger. I am the heir of the one who has no heir: I pay the blood money on his behalf and I inherit from him. And the maternal uncle is the heir of the one who has no heir: he pays the blood money on his behalf and inherits from him."""
"6148","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever marries has completed half of his faith, so let him fear Allah regarding the remaining half."""
"6149","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever imitates a people is one of them."""
"6150","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever eats seven Ajwah dates every morning, neither poison nor magic will harm him on that day."""
"6151","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever gives something of his body in charity is given a reward in proportion to what he gave in charity."""
"6152","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever gives in charity the equivalent of one date from lawful earnings, and Allah accepts only what is pure, Allah accepts it with His right hand, then He makes it grow for its owner just as one of you raises his foal, until it becomes like a mountain."""
"6153","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever practises medicine without having any knowledge of medicine is liable for the harm."""
"6154","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever purifies himself in his house, then comes to the Quba Mosque and prays in it, will have a reward like that of an Umrah."""
"6155","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever purifies himself in his house, then walks to one of the houses of Allah in order to fulfil one of the obligations of Allah, one of his steps erases a sin and the other raises him a rank."""
"6156","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever wakes up at night and says as soon as he wakes: 'La ilaha illallahu wahdahu la sharika lah, lahul-mulku wa lahul-hamd, yuhyi wa yumitu, biyadihil-khayr, wa huwa 'ala kulli shay'in qadir. Subhanallah, wal-hamdu lillah, wa la ilaha illallah, wallahu akbar, wa la hawla wa la quwwata illa billah' (There is no true god except Allah, alone, without partner; to Him belongs the dominion and to Him belongs all praise; He gives life and causes death; in His hand is all good, and He has power over all things. Glory be to Allah, all praise is for Allah, there is no true god except Allah, Allah is the Greatest, and there is no might and no power except by Allah), then says: 'Allahummaghfir li' (O Allah, forgive me), or makes any other supplication, his supplication is answered. Then if he gets up, performs ablution and prays, his prayer is accepted."""
"6157","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever thinks himself great and walks arrogantly will meet Allah while He is angry with him."""
"6158","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever acquires knowledge in order to boast with it before the scholars, or to argue with the foolish, or to turn people's faces towards himself, Allah will admit him into Hell."""
"6159","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever learns knowledge by which the pleasure of Allah is sought, but learns it only to obtain some worldly gain, will not even find the fragrance of Paradise on the Day of Resurrection."""
"6160","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever spits towards the Qiblah will come on the Day of Resurrection with his spittle between his eyes. And whoever eats from this foul-smelling plant, let him not come near our mosque."""
"6161","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever attributes to me something I did not say, let him take his seat in the Fire."""
"6162","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever humbles himself for the sake of Allah, Allah raises him."""
"6163","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever performs ablution and does it well, then goes and finds that the people have already prayed, Allah gives him the same reward as the one who prayed it and attended it, without that diminishing anything from their reward."""
"6164","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever performs ablution and does it well, then says: 'Ashhadu an la ilaha illallahu wahdahu la sharika lah, wa ashhadu anna Muhammadan 'abduhu wa rasuluh' (I bear witness that there is no true god except Allah, alone, without partner, and I bear witness that Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) is His servant and Messenger), the gates of Paradise are opened for him, and he may enter through whichever of them he wishes."""
"6165","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever performs ablution and does it well, then prays two rak'ahs without any heedlessness in them, Allah forgives him his past sins."""
"6166","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever performs ablution and does it well, then prays two rak'ahs, turning to them fully with his heart and his face, Paradise becomes obligatory for him."""
"6167","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever performs ablution and does it well, then says: 'Ashhadu an la ilaha illallahu wahdahu la sharika lah, wa anna Muhammadan 'abduhu wa rasuluh. Allahummaj'alni minat-tawwabin, waj'alni minal-mutatahhirin' (I bear witness that there is no true god except Allah, alone, without partner, and that Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) is His servant and Messenger. O Allah, make me among those who repent often, and make me among those who purify themselves), all eight gates of Paradise are opened for him, and he may enter through whichever of them he wishes."""
"6168","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever performs ablution and does it well, then says: 'Ashhadu an la ilaha illallahu wahdahu la sharika lah, wa ashhadu anna Muhammadan 'abduhu wa rasuluh' (I bear witness that there is no true god except Allah, alone, without partner, and I bear witness that Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) is His servant and Messenger), the gates of Paradise are opened for him, and he may enter through whichever of them he wishes."""
"6169","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever performs ablution and does it well, his sins leave his body, until they even come out from beneath his nails."""
"6170","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever performs ablution and then, after finishing his ablution, says: O Allah, You are free from all imperfection, and all praise is Yours; I bear witness that there is no true god except You; I seek Your forgiveness and I turn to You in repentance, it is written on a sheet and then a seal is placed on it, which is not broken until the Day of Resurrection."""
"6171","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever performs ablution, let him blow out his nose; and whoever cleans himself with stones after relieving himself, let him use an odd number."""
"6172","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever performs ablution as he has been commanded and prays as he has been commanded, his previous deeds are forgiven."""
"6173","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever performs ablution for the prayer and completes it thoroughly, then walks to the obligatory prayer and prays it with the people, Allah forgives him his sins."""
"6174","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever performs ablution like this, then comes to the mosque, prays two rak'ahs and then sits, his past sins are forgiven. But do not be deceived by this."""
"6175","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever performs ablution like this ablution of mine, then stands and prays two rak'ahs in which his mind does not wander to anything else, his past sins are forgiven."""
"6176","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever performs ablution similar to this ablution of mine, then prays two rak'ahs in which his mind does not wander to anything else, his past sins are forgiven."""
"6177","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever performs ablution like this, then goes out to the mosque, with nothing but the prayer taking him there, his past sins are forgiven."""
"6178","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever performs ablution like this, his past sins are forgiven, and his prayer and his walking to the mosque are counted as voluntary."""
"6179","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever performs ablution on Friday and does it well, then comes to the Friday prayer, draws near and listens in silence, is forgiven what is between that and the next Friday, plus three more days. And whoever plays with the pebbles has engaged in idle talk."""
"6180","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever performs ablution on Friday, that is sufficient and good; and whoever takes a ritual bath (ghusl), the bath is better."""
"6181","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever takes as his patrons people other than his own masters has thrown off the collar of Islam from his neck."""
"6182","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever takes another people as his patrons without the permission of his masters, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels and all the people. Allah will not accept from him on the Day of Resurrection any voluntary deed or any obligatory one."""
"6183","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever keeps up twelve rak'ahs of the Sunnah, Allah builds for him a house in Paradise: four rak'ahs before Zuhr and two after it, two after Maghrib, two after Isha, and two before Fajr."""
"6184","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever comes to this mosque of mine, coming only for some good that he will learn or teach, he is at the rank of one who strives in the path of Allah. And whoever comes to it for any other purpose is like a man looking at someone else's belongings."""
"6185","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever comes worshipping Allah, not associating anything with Him, establishing the prayer, giving zakah, fasting Ramadan and avoiding the major sins, Paradise is his."" The Companions asked: ""What are the major sins?"" He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Associating partners with Allah, killing a Muslim soul, and fleeing on the day of battle."""
"6186","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever associates with a polytheist and lives with him is like him."""
"6187","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever lets his lower garment trail, intending nothing by it but arrogance, Allah will not look at him with mercy on the Day of Resurrection."""
"6188","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever lets his garment trail out of arrogance, Allah will not look at him with mercy on the Day of Resurrection."""
"6189","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever makes all his concerns a single concern, the concern for the Hereafter, Allah will suffice him for all his other concerns. And whoever is divided by concerns over worldly affairs, Allah does not care in which of its valleys he perishes."""
"6190","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever is appointed a judge among the people has, as it were, been slaughtered without a knife."""
"6191","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever drives the horses unlawfully on the day of the race is not one of us."""
"6192","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever sits in a gathering in which there is much idle talk, and then, before rising from that gathering, says: 'Subhanaka Allahumma rabbana wa bihamdika, ashhadu an la ilaha illa anta, astaghfiruka wa atubu ilayk' (O Allah, our Lord, You are free of all imperfection, and all praise is Yours; I bear witness that there is no true god except You; I seek Your forgiveness and turn to You in repentance), he is forgiven for what took place in that gathering."""
"6193","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever equips a fighter in the path of Allah, it is as though he himself has fought; and whoever looks after a fighter's family well, it is as though he himself has fought."""
"6194","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever equips a fighter in the path of Allah receives a reward like his, and that does not diminish the fighter's reward in any way."""
"6195","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever regularly observes four rak'ahs before Zuhr and four after it is made forbidden to the Hellfire."""
"6196","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever, through his intercession, obstructs the carrying out of one of the prescribed punishments (hudud) set by Allah has opposed Allah's command. Whoever dies while in debt, its settlement will not be with dinars and dirhams but with good deeds and bad deeds. Whoever knowingly disputes in support of falsehood remains under Allah's displeasure until he desists. And whoever says about a believer something that is not in him, Allah will make him dwell in the mire of the pus and blood of the people of Hell until he comes out of what he said, and he will not be able to come out of it."""
"6197","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever performs Hajj for the sake of Allah, and neither speaks obscenely nor commits sin, returns like the day his mother gave birth to him."""
"6198","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever performs Hajj to this House, his last act should be the circumambulation (tawaf) of the House."""
"6199","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever narrates a hadith from me which he considers to be a lie is himself one of the liars."""
"6200","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever digs a well, the area of forty cubits around it belongs to him as pasture for his livestock."""
"6201","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever memorises ten verses from the beginning of Surah al-Kahf will be protected from the trial of the Dajjal."""
"6202","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever guards what is between his jaws and what is between his legs will enter Paradise."""
"6203","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever swears by trust (amanah) is not one of us."""
"6204","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever swears by other than Allah has committed shirk."""
"6205","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever swears a sinful, false oath beside this pulpit of mine, let him take his seat in the Hellfire, even if it is over a green tooth-stick (miswak)."""
"6206","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever swears an oath and says 'In sha Allah (if Allah wills)', then if he wishes he may carry it out, and if he wishes he may leave it, and he will not bear the sin of breaking his oath."""
"6207","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever swears a binding oath to seize the wealth of a Muslim, while he is lying in it, will meet Allah while He is angry with him."""
"6208","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever swears an oath and then sees something better than it, let him do what is better and offer expiation for his oath."""
"6209","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever swears an oath and says 'In sha Allah (if Allah wills)' has made an exception."""
"6210","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever swears an oath and says 'In sha Allah (if Allah wills)' has the choice: if he wishes he may carry it out, and if he wishes he may leave it."""
"6211","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever swears an oath and says 'In sha Allah (if Allah wills)' has the choice: if he wishes he may carry it out, and if he wishes he may leave it, and he will not bear the sin of breaking his oath."""
"6212","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever swears an oath and says 'In sha Allah (if Allah wills)' bears no sin for breaking the oath."""
"6213","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever swears a binding oath, falsely and deliberately, in order to seize thereby the wealth of his Muslim brother, let him take his seat in the Hellfire."""
"6214","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever wishes to swear, let him swear by the Lord of the Ka'bah."""
"6215","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever swears an oath to cut off ties of kinship, or over something that is not right, his righteousness lies in not fulfilling it."""
"6216","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever among you, while swearing, says: 'By al-Lat and al-Uzza!', let him immediately say: 'La ilaha illallah' (There is no true god except Allah). And whoever says to his companion: 'Come, let me gamble with you', let him give something in charity as expiation for it."""
"6217","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever takes up arms against us is not one of us."""
"6218","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever takes up arms against us is not one of us, and whoever deceives us is not one of us either."""
"6219","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever is brought to account will be punished."""
"6220","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever is brought to account on the Day of Resurrection will be punished."" Sayyidah Aishah (may Allah be pleased with her) said: ""Does Allah Almighty not say: 'He will soon be given an easy reckoning'?"" He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""That is not a severe reckoning; that is merely the presentation of deeds. But whoever has his reckoning scrutinised will be destroyed."""
"6221","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever fears that he will not wake up in the last part of the night, let him pray witr at the beginning of the night; and whoever hopes to wake up in the last part of the night, let him pray witr in the last part of the night, for the prayer at the end of the night is attended by the angels, and that is better."""
"6222","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever fears danger travels by night, and whoever travels by night reaches the destination. Behold! The merchandise of Allah is costly. Behold! The merchandise of Allah is Paradise."""
"6223","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever turns a man's wife or his slave against him is not one of us."""
"6224","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever's life ends upon fasting a day will enter Paradise."""
"6225","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever sets out and comes to this mosque, that is, the Mosque of Quba, and prays in it, receives a reward equal to that of an Umrah."""
"6226","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever goes out with a funeral from its house, prays the funeral prayer over it, and then follows it until it is buried, receives two qirats of reward, each qirat being like Mount Uhud. And whoever prays over it and then returns receives a reward like Mount Uhud."""
"6227","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever leaves obedience to the ruler and separates from the Jama'ah (main body of the Muslims), and then dies, dies a death of Jahiliyyah (pre-Islamic ignorance). Whoever fights under the banner of blind partisanship, becoming angry for the sake of partisanship, calling to partisanship or supporting partisanship, and is then killed, his killing is a killing of Jahiliyyah. And whoever rises against my Ummah, striking both its righteous and its wicked, not sparing even its believers, and not fulfilling the covenant of the one with whom a covenant was made, he is not of me and I am not of him."""
"6228","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever goes out from his house in a state of purity for an obligatory prayer, his reward is like the reward of a pilgrim in ihram. Whoever goes out for the Duha prayer, intending nothing but that, his reward is like the reward of one performing Umrah. And one prayer after another, with no idle talk between them, is recorded in Illiyyin."""
"6229","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever withdraws his hand from obedience (to the leader) will meet Allah on the Day of Resurrection with no argument in his favour; and whoever dies with no pledge of allegiance (bay'ah) upon his neck dies a death of Jahiliyyah (pre-Islamic ignorance)."""
"6230","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whomever Allah Almighty has created for one of the two abodes, He grants him the ability to do its deeds."""
"6231","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever enters the market and says: 'La ilaha illallahu wahdahu la sharika lah, lahul-mulku wa lahul-hamd, yuhyi wa yumit, wa huwa hayyun la yamut, biyadihil-khayr, wa huwa ala kulli shay'in qadir' (There is no true god except Allah alone, He has no partner; His is the dominion and His is all praise; He gives life and causes death; He is Ever-Living and will not die; all good is in His hand, and He has power over all things), Allah will record for him a million good deeds, erase from him a million sins, raise him a million degrees, and build for him a house in Paradise."""
"6232","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever enters an orchard may eat, but let him not hide anything away (to take with him)."""
"6233","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever enters this mosque and spits or brings up phlegm in it, let him dig a hole and bury it. If he cannot do that, let him spit into his garment and then take it out with him."""
"6234","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever calls to guidance will have a reward like the rewards of those who follow him, without that diminishing their rewards in any way. And whoever calls to misguidance will bear a sin like the sins of those who follow him, without that diminishing their sins in any way."""
"6235","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever supplicates for his brother in his absence, the angel appointed over him says: 'Amin, and for you the like of it (be granted).'"""
"6236","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever is invited to a meal while he is fasting, let him accept; then, if he wishes, he may eat, and if he wishes, he may leave it."""
"6237","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever is invited to a wedding or to some other invitation like it, let him accept."""
"6238","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever buries three of his children, Allah Almighty will make the Fire forbidden for him."""
"6239","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever guides someone to a good deed will receive a reward like that of the one who does it."""
"6240","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever defends his brother's honour against backbiting, it is a right upon Allah Almighty that He free him from the Fire."""
"6241","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever slaughters (his sacrifice) after the prayer, his sacrifice is complete and he has attained the way of the Muslims."""
"6242","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever slaughters (his sacrifice) before the prayer, slaughters only for himself; and whoever slaughters after the prayer, his sacrifice is complete and he has attained the way of the Muslims."""
"6243","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever is overcome by vomiting (involuntarily) while fasting, there is no make-up due from him; and whoever makes himself vomit, let him make it up."""
"6244","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever mentions a man with something that is truly found in him has backbitten him."""
"6245","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever I am mentioned in front of and he falls short in sending blessings upon me has missed the path to Paradise."""
"6246","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever I am mentioned in front of, let him send blessings upon me, for whoever sends blessings upon me once, Allah Almighty sends mercy upon him ten times."""
"6247","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever sees a snake and does not kill it out of fear of its pursuit is not one of us."""
"6248","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever sees someone afflicted and says: 'Alhamdu lillahilladhi 'afani mimmabtalaka bihi wa faddalani 'ala kathirin mimman khalaqa tafdila' (All praise is for Allah, who has kept me safe from that with which He has afflicted you, and has favoured me over much of His creation), that affliction will never reach him."""
"6249","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever sees something he dislikes from his ruler, let him be patient with it, for whoever separates from the community (jama'ah) even by a handspan and dies, dies the death of the Days of Ignorance (Jahiliyyah)."""
"6250","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever among you sees an evil, let him change it with his hand; if he is not able to, then with his tongue; and if he is not able to do even that, then with his heart (by hating it), and that is the weakest degree of faith."""
"6251","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever sees the new moon of Dhu al-Hijjah and intends to offer a sacrifice, let him not cut his hair or his nails until he has offered the sacrifice."""
"6252","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever sees me (in a dream), then he has truly seen me, for Satan cannot take on my form."""
"6253","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever has seen me (in a dream) has seen the truth, for Satan cannot make himself look like me."""
"6254","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever has seen me (in a dream) has seen the truth, for Satan cannot make himself look like me."""
"6255","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever sees me in a dream will soon see me while awake as well, and Satan cannot take on my form."""
"6256","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever sees me in a dream has truly seen me, for it is not possible for Satan to take on my appearance."""
"6257","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever sees me in a dream has truly seen me, for Satan cannot take on my form."""
"6258","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whichever woman among you sees that (in a dream) and has a discharge (of fluid), let her perform the ritual bath (ghusl)."""
"6259","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever stands guard (on the frontier) for a day and a night in the path of Allah will have a reward like that of fasting a month and standing (in prayer) during it; and whoever dies while standing guard, this same reward will continue for him, his provision will also continue, and he will be safe from the one who puts to trial (the questioning angels)."""
"6260","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever goes out in the evening in the path of Allah (for jihad), he will be given, on the Day of Resurrection, musk (in fragrance) equal to the dust that touched him."""
"6261","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever shows mercy, even if it is to a sparrow being slaughtered, Allah Almighty will show him mercy on the Day of Resurrection."""
"6262","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever defends the honour of his brother, Allah Almighty will keep the Fire away from his face on the Day of Resurrection."""
"6263","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever defends the honour of his brother, it will be a screen of protection for him from the Fire."""
"6264","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever is held back from (fulfilling) his need by an evil omen has committed shirk."""
"6265","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever removes a stone from the road, a good deed is recorded for him, and whoever has a good deed will enter Paradise."""
"6266","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever prays twelve rak'ahs (of voluntary prayer), a house is built for him in Paradise."""
"6267","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever shoots an arrow at the enemy in the path of Allah and his arrow reaches the enemy, whether it hits the mark or misses, this is equal to freeing a slave."""
"6268","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever shoots an arrow in the path of Allah, this is for him equal to freeing a slave."""
"6269","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever accuses a believer of disbelief, it is like killing him."""
"6270","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever shoots arrows at us (or attacks us) by night is not one of us."""
"6271","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever visits a people as a guest, let him not lead them in prayer; rather, let a man from among them lead them."""
"6272","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever cultivates land without the permission of its owners will get only his expenses, and he will have no share in the crop."""
"6273","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever plants a crop and a bird or some creature eats from it, it is charity for him."""
"6274","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever commits fornication, faith leaves him; then if he repents, Allah Almighty accepts his repentance."""
"6275","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever asks Allah for Paradise three times, Paradise says: 'O Allah, admit him into Paradise'; and whoever seeks protection from the Fire three times, the Fire says: 'O Allah, protect him from the Fire.'"""
"6276","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever sincerely asks Allah for martyrdom, Allah Almighty will raise him to the ranks of the martyrs, even if he dies on his bed."""
"6277","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever, with sincerity of heart, asks to be killed in the path of Allah, Allah Almighty will grant him the reward of a martyr, even if he dies on his bed."""
"6278","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever asks people for their wealth in order to increase his own is in effect asking for embers of Hell, so let him ask for little or for much."""
"6279","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever asks people while he has what would make him self-sufficient will come on the Day of Resurrection with his asking appearing on his face as scratches or wounds."" It was said: ""What is self-sufficiency?"" He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Fifty dirhams or its equivalent in gold."""
"6280","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever asks for something while he has what would make him self-sufficient is in effect asking for more embers of Hell."" The Companions said: ""What makes him self-sufficient?"" He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""As much as provides him his morning and evening meals."""
"6281","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever begs without (the need of) poverty, it is as though he is eating embers."""
"6282","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever has forty dirhams and still asks is one who burdens people (with importunity)."""
"6283","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever has the value of one uqiyah and still asks has been importunate (a burden) in his asking."""
"6284","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever is asked about some knowledge and conceals it, Allah Almighty will bridle him on the Day of Resurrection with a bridle of fire."""
"6285","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever reviles my Companions (speaks ill of them), upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels and all the people."""
"6286","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever says Subhan Allah thirty-three times, Alhamdu lillah thirty-three times and Allahu Akbar thirty-three times after every prayer, making ninety-nine, and then, to complete the hundred, says: 'La ilaha illallahu wahdahu la sharika lahu, lahul-mulku wa lahul-hamdu wa huwa 'ala kulli shay'in qadir' (There is no true god except Allah, He is alone, He has no partner; His is the dominion, His is all praise, and He has power over all things), his sins are forgiven even if they are like the foam of the sea."""
"6287","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever covers (the faults of) his Muslim brother in this world, Allah Almighty will cover him on the Day of Resurrection."""
"6288","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever would love to find the sweetness of faith, let him love a person solely for the sake of Allah."""
"6289","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever would love to love Allah and His Messenger, let him recite from the Qur'an."""
"6290","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever would love Allah Almighty to answer his prayers in times of hardship and distress, let him supplicate abundantly in times of ease."""
"6291","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever would love Allah Almighty to increase his provision and lengthen his life, let him maintain ties of kinship."""
"6292","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever would be pleased to look at the humility and modesty of Isa (peace be upon him), let him look at Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him)."""
"6293","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever would be pleased to see the Day of Resurrection as though he were seeing it with his own eyes, let him recite Surah at-Takwir (When the sun is wrapped up [and its light is gone]), Surah al-Infitar (When the sky breaks apart) and Surah al-Inshiqaq (When the sky is split open)."""
"6294","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever is gladdened by his good deed and saddened by his bad deed is a believer."""
"6295","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever has something stolen and finds his stolen property with a man who is not suspected of theft, then if he wishes he may take it by paying its price, and if he wishes he may pursue the original thief."""
"6296","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever lives in the desert (the Bedouin life) becomes hard-hearted, whoever keeps chasing game becomes heedless, and whoever frequents the ruler falls into trial (fitnah)."""
"6297","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever travels a path in which he seeks knowledge, Allah Almighty makes easy for him, by means of it, one of the paths of Paradise. The angels lower their wings for the seeker of knowledge, pleased with what he does. The creatures in the heavens and on the earth, even the fish in the water, seek forgiveness for the scholar. The superiority of the scholar over the worshipper is like the superiority of the moon on the night of the full moon over all the other stars. The scholars are the heirs of the prophets, and the prophets did not leave behind a dinar or a dirham as inheritance; rather, they left knowledge as their inheritance, so whoever takes it has taken an abundant share."""
"6298","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever travels a path in which he seeks knowledge, Allah Almighty makes easy for him a path to Paradise."""
"6299","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever draws the sword against us is not one of us."""
"6300","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever hears the call to prayer (adhan) and does not come to the mosque, there is no prayer for him, unless he has an excuse."""
"6301","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever hears of the Dajjal, let him keep away from him, for by Allah! A man will come to him thinking that he is a believer, then he will follow him because of the doubts he spreads."""
"6302","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever hears a man announcing a lost item in the mosque, let him say: 'May Allah not return it to you,' for the mosques were not built for this purpose."""
"6303","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever does his deeds for fame, Allah Almighty will make him famous (will disgrace him), and whoever does them for show, Allah Almighty will put him on show (will disgrace him)."""
"6304","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever does his deeds for fame, Allah Almighty will make him famous (disgrace him); whoever does them for show, Allah Almighty will put him on show; and whoever makes things difficult for people, Allah Almighty will make things difficult for him on the Day of Resurrection."""
"6305","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever introduces a good practice in Islam will have its reward and the reward of those who act upon it after him, without anything being reduced from their rewards; and whoever introduces an evil practice in Islam will bear its sin and the sin of those who act upon it after him, without anything being reduced from their sins."""
"6306","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever introduces a good practice that is acted upon after him will have its reward and the like of their reward, without anything being reduced from their rewards; and whoever introduces an evil practice that is acted upon after him will bear its sin and the like of their sins, without anything being reduced from their sins."""
"6307","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever has even a single hair turn white on his head while in Islam, it will be a light for him on the Day of Resurrection."""
"6308","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever has even a single hair turn white on his head in the path of Allah, it will be a light for him on the Day of Resurrection."""
"6309","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever drinks wine, flog him; then if he drinks again, flog him; then if he drinks a third time, flog him; then if he drinks a fourth time, kill him."""
"6310","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever drinks wine in this world and does not repent from it, it will be forbidden to him in the Hereafter."""
"6311","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever drinks wine in this world will not drink it in the Hereafter."""
"6312","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever drinks wine, his prayer is not accepted for forty days. Then if he repents, Allah Almighty accepts his repentance. Then if he returns to it, his prayer is not accepted for forty days. Then if he repents, Allah Almighty accepts his repentance. Then if he returns to it, his prayer is not accepted for forty days. Then if he repents, Allah Almighty accepts his repentance. Then if he returns to it a fourth time, his prayer is not accepted for forty days, and if he repents this time, Allah Almighty does not accept his repentance, and He will give him to drink from the river of Khabal."""
"6313","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever drinks wine and becomes intoxicated, his prayer is not accepted for forty days; if he dies, he will enter the Fire, and if he repents, Allah Almighty accepts his repentance. Then if he again drinks wine and becomes intoxicated, his prayer is not accepted for forty days; if he dies, he will enter the Fire, and if he repents, Allah Almighty accepts his repentance. Then if he again drinks wine and becomes intoxicated, his prayer is not accepted for forty days; if he dies, he will enter the Fire, and if he repents, Allah Almighty accepts his repentance. But if he returns yet again, it becomes a right upon Allah Almighty that He give him to drink, on the Day of Resurrection, from Radghat al-Khabal, that is, the pus (the discharge) of the people of Hell."""
"6314","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever drinks from a vessel of silver, it is as though he is pouring the fire of Hell into his stomach."""
"6315","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever drinks from a vessel of gold or silver, it is as though he is pouring the fire of Hell into his stomach."""
"6316","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever intercedes for his brother, and he gives him a gift for it and he accepts it, has entered one of the great doors of usury (riba)."""
"6317","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever attends a funeral until the prayer is offered over it will have one qirat of reward, and whoever remains present until it is buried will have two qirats, like two great mountains."""
"6318","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever bears witness that ""La ilaha illallah"" (there is no god worthy of worship except Allah) will enter Paradise."""
"6319","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever bears witness that ""La ilaha illallah wa anna Muhammadan rasulullah"" (there is no god worthy of worship except Allah, and Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) is the Messenger of Allah), Allah Almighty will forbid the Fire for him."""
"6320","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever bears witness that ""La ilaha illallah wahdahu la sharika lahu wa anna Muhammadan abduhu wa rasuluh"" (there is no god worthy of worship except Allah, He is alone and has no partner, and Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) is His servant and Messenger), and that Isa (peace be upon him) is His servant and Messenger, the son of His female servant (Maryam), and His word which He cast to Maryam, and a spirit from Him, and that Paradise is true, Hell is true and the resurrection is true, Allah Almighty will admit him into Paradise through whichever of the eight gates of Paradise he wishes, whatever his deeds may have been."""
"6321","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever attends this prayer of ours and stays with us until we depart, having already stood at Arafat before that, by night or by day, his Hajj is complete and he has removed his unkemptness (of ihram)."""
"6322","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever unsheathes his sword and then strikes with it, his blood is shed with impunity."""
"6323","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever fasts perpetually (without a break) has neither fasted nor broken his fast."""
"6324","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever fasts three days of every month, it is as though he has fasted perpetually."""
"6325","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever fasts Ramadan out of faith and seeking reward (with the intention of earning reward), all his past and future sins are forgiven."""
"6326","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever fasts Ramadan out of faith and seeking reward (with the intention of earning reward), all his past sins are forgiven."""
"6327","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever fasts Ramadan and then follows it with six fasts of Shawwal, it is as though he has fasted perpetually."""
"6328","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever fasts six days after Eid al-Fitr, it is equal to fasting the whole year, because (Allah Almighty says:) Whoever brings a good deed will have ten times its like."""
"6329","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever fasts one day in the path of Allah, Allah Almighty, because of that one day, will keep the heat of Hell away from his face the distance of seventy years."""
"6330","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever fasts one day in the path of Allah, Allah Almighty will keep Hell away from him the distance of a hundred years' journey."""
"6331","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever fasts one day in the path of Allah, Allah Almighty will keep his face away from Hell the distance of seventy years."""
"6332","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever fasts one day in the path of Allah, Allah Almighty will keep his face away from the Fire the distance of seventy years."""
"6333","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever fasts one day in the path of Allah, Allah Almighty will place between him and the Fire a trench as wide as the distance between the heaven and the earth."""
"6334","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever fasts one day in the path of Allah, Allah Almighty, because of that one day, will move his face away from the Fire the distance of seventy years."""
"6335","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever fasts the day of Arafah, Allah Almighty forgives his sins of two years: one year ahead and one year behind."""
"6336","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever falls from his mount and dies is a martyr."""
"6337","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever prays the prayers of the two cool times (Fajr and Asr) will enter Paradise."""
"6338","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever prays the morning prayer is under the protection of Allah, so beware! Let not Allah Almighty demand anything from you concerning His protection."""
"6339","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever prays the morning prayer is under the protection of Allah. Beware! Let not Allah Almighty demand anything from you concerning His protection, for whomever Allah Almighty demands anything from concerning His protection, He will seize him and then throw him on his face into the fire of Hell."""
"6340","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever prays four rak'ahs of the forenoon prayer (Duha) and four rak'ahs before the Zuhr prayer, a house is built for him in Paradise."""
"6341","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever prays the Isha prayer in congregation, it is as though he stood in prayer for half the night, and whoever prays the Fajr prayer in congregation, it is as though he prayed the whole night."""
"6342","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever prays Isha in congregation, it is as if he stood in prayer for half the night; and whoever prays both Isha and Fajr in congregation, it is as if he stood in prayer for the whole night."""
"6343","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever prays the morning prayer remains under the protection of Allah until evening."""
"6344","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever prays Fajr is under the protection of Allah. Beware, lest Allah Almighty demand anything from you concerning His protection."""
"6345","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever prays Fajr is under the protection of Allah, and his reckoning rests with Allah."""
"6346","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever prays Fajr in congregation, then remains remembering Allah until the sun rises, then prays two rak'ahs, will have the reward of a complete Hajj and Umrah: complete, complete, complete."""
"6347","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever has prayed one rak'ah of Fajr and then the sun rises, let him complete the rest of Fajr."""
"6348","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever prays a prayer and does not complete it, it is supplemented from his voluntary prayers until it becomes complete."""
"6349","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever prays a prayer in which he does not recite Surah al-Fatihah, it is deficient, deficient, deficient, not complete."""
"6350","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever prays our prayer, faces our qiblah and eats what we slaughter, that is the Muslim who has the protection of Allah and the protection of His Messenger. So do not betray Allah with regard to anyone under His protection."""
"6351","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever prays our prayer and offers the sacrifice according to our way has made his sacrifice correctly; and whoever sacrifices before the prayer, there is no sacrifice for him."""
"6352","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever offers the funeral prayer will receive one qirat; and if he also attends the burial, he will receive two qirats. And one qirat is like the mountain of Uhud."""
"6353","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever offers the funeral prayer will receive one qirat; and whoever waits until the deceased is placed in the grave-niche will receive two qirats. And the two qirats are like two great mountains."""
"6354","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever offers the funeral prayer in the mosque will receive no reward."""
"6355","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever offers the funeral prayer and does not follow the funeral procession will receive one qirat; and if he follows it, he will receive two qirats."""
"6356","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever has the funeral prayer offered over him by a hundred Muslims will be forgiven."""
"6357","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever sends blessings upon me ten times in the morning and ten times in the evening will attain my intercession on the Day of Resurrection."""
"6358","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever sends blessings upon me once, Allah Almighty sends mercy upon him ten times in return for it."""
"6359","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever sends blessings upon me once, Allah Almighty sends mercy upon him ten times, wipes away ten of his sins and raises him ten degrees."""
"6360","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever prays twelve voluntary rak'ahs in a day and night, Allah Almighty builds for him a house in Paradise."""
"6361","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever prays in a single garment, let him cross its two ends over his opposite shoulders."""
"6362","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever prays twelve rak'ahs in a day and night, a house is built for him in Paradise: four rak'ahs before Zuhr, two after it, two after Maghrib, two after Isha and two before the Fajr prayer."""
"6363","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever prays standing, that is superior; whoever prays sitting will have half the reward of the one standing; and whoever prays lying down will have half the reward of the one sitting."""
"6364","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever prays four rak'ahs before Zuhr and four after it, Allah Almighty will make him forbidden to the Fire."""
"6365","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever prays for Allah's sake in congregation for forty days, catching the opening takbir, two exemptions are written for him: exemption from the Fire and exemption from hypocrisy."""
"6366","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever prays and then remains sitting, waiting for the next prayer, is counted as being in prayer until the prayer he is awaiting comes to him."""
"6367","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever remains silent is saved."""
"6368","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever has a kindness done to him and says to the one who did it: 'Jazak Allahu khayran' (May Allah reward you with good), has reached the utmost in praise."""
"6369","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever does something that is not in accordance with our way, it is rejected."""
"6370","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever makes an image, Allah Almighty will punish him with it on the Day of Resurrection until he breathes a soul into it, and he will not be able to breathe one into it. Whoever falsely relates a dream will be made to tie a knot between two barley grains, and he will not be able to tie it. And whoever eavesdrops on the conversation of people who flee from him, molten lead will be poured into his ears on the Day of Resurrection."""
"6371","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever makes an image in this world will be made to breathe a soul into it on the Day of Resurrection, and he will not be able to do so."""
"6372","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever harms another, Allah Almighty will harm him; and whoever creates hardship for another, Allah Almighty will create hardship for him."""
"6373","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever offers his sacrifice before the prayer has only slaughtered for himself; and whoever slaughters after the prayer, his sacrifice is complete and he has attained the way of the Muslims."""
"6374","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever unjustly strikes someone with a whip, retribution will be taken from him on the Day of Resurrection."""
"6375","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever beats his slave as a punishment for something he did not commit, or slaps him, its expiation is that he sets him free."""
"6376","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever unjustly beats his slave, retribution will be taken from him on the Day of Resurrection."""
"6377","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever's heart is unwilling to spend wealth and to bear the hardship of worship at night, let him keep saying 'Subhan Allahi wa bihamdihi' (Glory be to Allah, and praise be to Him)."""
"6378","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever wrongfully encroaches upon someone's dwelling, or blocks the road, or harms a believer, no jihad will be counted for him."""
"6379","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever performs tawaf of the House seven circuits and prays two rak'ahs, it is equal to freeing a slave."""
"6380","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever performs tawaf of this House seven circuits and keeps count of it, it is equal to freeing a slave. Whenever he puts down one foot and lifts the other, Allah Almighty wipes away a sin from him because of it and records a good deed for him."""
"6381","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever sincerely seeks martyrdom will be given its reward, even if it does not befall him."""
"6382","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever seeks knowledge in order to boast before the scholars, or to argue with the foolish, or to turn people's attention towards himself, he is in the Fire."""
"6383","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever seeks knowledge in order to compete with the scholars, or to argue with the foolish, or to turn people's attention towards himself, Allah Almighty will admit him into the Fire."""
"6384","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever seeks his right, let him seek it with decency and restraint, whether he receives it in full or not."""
"6385","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever unjustly takes even a hand-span of land, it will be hung around his neck as a collar from seven earths."""
"6386","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever shows enmity to Ammar (may Allah be pleased with him), Allah Almighty will show enmity to him; and whoever hates Ammar, Allah Almighty will hate him."""
"6387","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever visits a sick person, or visits a brother of his for the sake of Allah, a caller calls out to him: 'You have done well, your walking has been good, and you have taken up a dwelling in Paradise.'"""
"6388","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever visits a sick person whose appointed time of death has not yet come and says seven times in his presence: 'I ask Allah the Magnificent, Lord of the Magnificent Throne, to cure you,' Allah Almighty will cure him of that illness."""
"6389","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever visits a sick person remains in the khurfah (the fruit-gathering place) of Paradise until he returns."""
"6390","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever seeks refuge with Allah has sought refuge in a true refuge."""
"6391","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever raises two girls until they reach maturity, he and I will enter Paradise together like these two (fingers are together)."""
"6392","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever is offered a flower (a fragrant plant) should not refuse it, for it is light to carry and pleasant in fragrance."""
"6393","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever is offered perfume should not refuse it, for it is light to carry and fragrant."""
"6394","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever hangs an amulet has committed shirk (associated partners with Allah)."""
"6395","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever learns archery and then abandons it is not one of us."""
"6396","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever teaches some knowledge will have a reward equal to that of the one who acts upon it, and the reward of the one who acts upon it will not be diminished in the least."""
"6397","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever of my Ummah reaches the age of seventy years, Allah Almighty has left him no excuse regarding (the length of his) life."""
"6398","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever does a deed that is not in accordance with our way, it is rejected."""
"6399","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever goes to the mosque in the morning and in the evening, Allah Almighty prepares for him a hospitality in Paradise every time he goes in the morning or the evening."""
"6400","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever plants a plant, and a human being or any of Allah's creatures eats from it, it is charity for him."""
"6401","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever fights in the path of Allah while intending nothing but a rope (a worldly gain) will get only what he intended."""
"6402","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever washes the deceased should himself take a ritual bath (ghusl), and whoever carries him should perform ablution (wudu)."""
"6403","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever washes the deceased and conceals (his faults), Allah Almighty will cover him from sins, and whoever shrouds him, Allah Almighty will clothe him in the silk of Paradise."""
"6404","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever washes the deceased should himself take a ritual bath (ghusl)."""
"6405","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever washes his head and takes a ritual bath (ghusl) on Friday, then sets out early and arrives first, goes on foot and does not ride, sits close to the imam, listens attentively, remains silent and does not engage in idle talk, will have, for every step he takes from his house to the mosque, the reward of a year's fasting and its night prayer."""
"6406","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever cheats is not one of us."""
"6407","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever cheats us is not one of us."""
"6408","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever cheats us is not one of us, and the one who schemes and deceives is in the Fire."""
"6409","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever misappropriates a camel or a goat from the spoils of war will come on the Day of Resurrection carrying it."""
"6410","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever separates from the Jama'ah (the community) even by a hand-span has thrown off the collar of Islam from his neck."""
"6411","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever's soul leaves his body while he is free of three things will enter Paradise: arrogance, debt, and misappropriation (of spoils)."""
"6412","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever separates a mother from her child, Allah Almighty will separate him from his loved ones on the Day of Resurrection."""
"6413","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever sets out in the path of Allah and dies, or is killed, or his horse or camel throws him and breaks his neck, or a venomous creature stings him, or he dies on his bed by any death Allah wills, he is a martyr and Paradise is his."""
"6414","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever provides a fasting person with food to break his fast, or equips a fighter (for jihad), will have a reward equal to his."""
"6415","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever provides a fasting person with food to break his fast will have a reward equal to his, yet this will not diminish the reward of the fasting person in the least."""
"6416","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever fights in the path of Allah for as short a time as it takes to milk a she-camel, Paradise becomes obligatory for him. Whoever sincerely, from his heart, asks Allah for martyrdom in the path of Allah and then dies or is killed will have the reward of a martyr. Whoever receives a wound or suffers an injury in the path of Allah, it will come on the Day of Resurrection in its freshest state; its colour will be like saffron and its fragrance like musk. And whoever develops a boil in the path of Allah will bear the seal of the martyrs."""
"6417","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever fights so that the word of Allah is the highest is in the path of Allah."""
"6418","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever says in the morning: 'La ilaha illallahu wahdahu la sharika lah, lahul-mulku wa lahul-hamdu wa huwa 'ala kulli shay'in qadir' (There is no true god except Allah, alone, without partner; His is the dominion, to Him belongs all praise, and He has power over all things), it will be equal to freeing a slave from the descendants of Isma'il (peace be upon him); ten good deeds are recorded for him, ten sins are erased, he is raised ten ranks, and he remains protected from Satan until evening. And if he says it in the evening, he gets the same until morning."""
"6419","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever says when leaving his house: 'Bismillah, tawakkaltu 'alallah, la hawla wa la quwwata illa billah' (In the name of Allah, I place my trust in Allah; there is no power to avoid evil nor strength to do good except with the help of Allah), it is said to him: 'You have been sufficed and you have been protected,' and Satan moves away from him."""
"6420","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever says, 'I am better than Yunus bin Matta,' has lied."""
"6421","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever says, 'I am free of Islam': if he is lying, he is as he said, and if he is truthful, he will not return to Islam safely."""
"6422","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever says upon hearing the mu'adhdhin: 'Wa ana ashhadu an la ilaha illallahu wahdahu la sharika lah, wa ashhadu anna Muhammadan 'abduhu wa rasuluh, raditu billahi rabban, wa bi-Muhammadin rasulan, wa bil-Islami dinan' (And I too bear witness that there is no true god except Allah, alone, without partner, and I bear witness that Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) is His servant and Messenger; I am pleased with Allah as Lord, with Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) as Messenger, and with Islam as religion), Allah Almighty forgives his past sins."""
"6423","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever recites this supplication upon hearing the call to prayer: 'O Allah, Lord of this perfect call and of the prayer about to be established, grant Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) al-Wasilah and virtue, and raise him to the Praised Station (al-Maqam al-Mahmud) which You have promised him,' my intercession becomes due for him on the Day of Resurrection."""
"6424","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever recites this supplication in the morning or in the evening: 'O Allah, You are my Lord; there is no true god except You. You created me and I am Your servant, and I abide by Your covenant and promise as much as I am able. I seek refuge in You from the evil of what I have done. I acknowledge Your favour upon me and I acknowledge my sin, so forgive me, for none forgives sins except You,' and then dies on that day or that night, will enter Paradise."""
"6425","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever says 'Subhanallahil-'azimi wa bihamdih' (Glory be to Allah, the Magnificent, and with His praise) one hundred times in the morning and in the evening, no one will come on the Day of Resurrection with a better deed than his, except someone who said the same and added to it."""
"6426","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever says three times in the evening: 'In the name of Allah, with whose name nothing on earth or in the heavens can cause harm, and He is the All-Hearing, the All-Knowing,' will not be struck by any sudden calamity until morning; and whoever says it three times in the morning will not be struck by any sudden calamity until evening."""
"6427","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever says three times in the evening: 'I seek refuge in the perfect words of Allah from the evil of what He has created,' a snake bite will not harm him that night."""
"6428","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever says: 'I am pleased with Allah as Lord, with Islam as religion, and with Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) as Prophet,' Paradise becomes obligatory for him."""
"6429","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever says: 'Subhanallahil-'azimi wa bihamdih' (Glory be to Allah, the Magnificent, with His praise), a date palm is planted for him in Paradise in return for it."""
"6430","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever says: 'Subhanallahi wa bihamdihi, subhanakallahumma wa bihamdika, ashhadu an la ilaha illa anta, astaghfiruka wa atubu ilayk' (Glory be to Allah and with His praise; glory be to You, O Allah, and with Your praise; I bear witness that there is no true god except You; I seek Your forgiveness and I turn to You in repentance): if he says it in a gathering of remembrance, it is as though a seal is set upon it, and if he says it in a gathering of idle talk, it becomes an expiation for him."""
"6431","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever says 'Subhanallahi wa bihamdih' (Glory be to Allah, and with His praise) one hundred times in a day, his sins are wiped away, even if they are like the foam of the sea."""
"6432","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever says to his companion on Friday, while the imam is delivering the sermon, 'Be quiet,' has engaged in idle talk."""
"6433","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever says 'La ilaha illallah' (There is no true god except Allah) sincerely from the heart will enter Paradise."""
"6434","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever says 'La ilaha illallah' (There is no true god except Allah), that word will surely benefit him on some day of his life, whatever may have befallen him before that."""
"6435","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever says ten times: 'La ilaha illallahu wahdahu la sharika lah, lahul-mulku wa lahul-hamdu wa huwa 'ala kulli shay'in qadir' (There is no true god except Allah, alone, without partner; His is the dominion, to Him belongs all praise, and He has power over all things), it is as though he freed a slave from the descendants of Isma'il (peace be upon him)."""
"6436","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever says ten times: 'La ilaha illallahu wahdahu la sharika lah, lahul-mulku wa lahul-hamdu, wa huwa 'ala kulli shay'in qadir' (There is no true god except Allah, alone, without partner; His is the dominion, to Him belongs all praise, and He has power over all things), it is for him equal to freeing a soul (a slave)."""
"6437","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever says one hundred times in a day: 'La ilaha illallahu wahdahu la sharika lah, lahul-mulku wa lahul-hamdu wa huwa 'ala kulli shay'in qadir' (There is no true god except Allah, alone, without partner; His is the dominion, to Him belongs all praise, and He has power over all things), it is for him equal to freeing ten slaves; one hundred good deeds are recorded for him, one hundred of his sins are erased, and it becomes a protection for him from Satan that day until evening; and no one brings a better deed than his, except someone who has done more than that."""
"6438","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever says 'La ilaha illallah' (There is no true god except Allah) and disbelieves in whatever is worshipped besides Allah, his wealth and his blood become inviolable (protected), and his reckoning rests with Allah, the Mighty and Majestic."""
"6439","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever recites ten verses in the night prayer is not recorded among the heedless; whoever recites one hundred verses is recorded among the devoutly obedient; and whoever recites one thousand verses is recorded among those who earn heaps of reward."""
"6440","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever stands (in prayer) in Ramadan out of faith and seeking reward, his past sins are forgiven."""
"6441","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever stands (in prayer) on Laylat al-Qadr (the Night of Decree) out of faith and seeking reward, his past sins are forgiven."""
"6442","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever is killed under a blind (aimless) banner, supporting partisanship (asabiyyah) and becoming angry for the sake of partisanship, his death is a death of Jahiliyyah (pre-Islamic ignorance)."""
"6443","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever is killed by mistake, his blood money (diyah) is one hundred camels: thirty bint makhad (one-year-old she-camels), thirty bint labun (two-year-old she-camels), thirty hiqqah (three-year-old she-camels) and ten banu labun (two-year-old male camels)."""
"6444","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever is killed while defending his wealth is a martyr."""
"6445","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever is killed while defending his wealth is a martyr, whoever is killed while defending his life is a martyr, whoever is killed while defending his religion is a martyr, and whoever is killed while defending his family is a martyr."""
"6446","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever is killed unjustly while defending his wealth, for him is Paradise."""
"6447","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever is killed while resisting the injustice being done to him is a martyr."""
"6448","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever kills a dhimmi (a non-Muslim under covenant) will not even find the fragrance of Paradise, although its fragrance can be perceived from a distance of seventy years' travel."""
"6449","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever is killed in the path of Allah is a martyr, whoever dies in the path of Allah is a martyr, whoever dies of the plague is a martyr, whoever dies of an abdominal illness is a martyr, and whoever dies by drowning is a martyr."""
"6450","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever is killed in a blind fight, or in a clash of stone-throwing and whips that takes place among people, his blood money is the blood money for accidental killing. And whoever kills deliberately, retribution (qisas) will be taken from him, and whoever stands between him and retribution, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels and all the people."""
"6451","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever is killed in a blind fight in which people strike with stones, whips or a stick, that is accidental, and his blood money is the blood money for accidental killing. And whoever kills deliberately, retribution (qisas) will be taken from him, and whoever prevents him from retribution, upon him is the curse of Allah and His wrath, and neither any voluntary deed nor any obligatory deed of his will be accepted."""
"6452","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever kills a disbeliever, his belongings (salab) are for him."""
"6453","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever has a relative killed has the choice of the better of two options: either he takes retribution (qisas), or he takes the blood money and forgives."""
"6454","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever kills a believer and rejoices at his killing, Allah Almighty will accept from him neither any voluntary deed nor any obligatory one."""
"6455","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever kills deliberately is to be handed over to the heirs of the slain person; if they wish they may take retribution, and if they wish they may take the blood money, which is: thirty hiqqah, thirty jadha'ah and forty pregnant she-camels. And whatever they settle upon is their right."""
"6456","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever kills a mu'ahad (a non-Muslim under covenant) unjustly, Allah Almighty will make Paradise forbidden for him."""
"6457","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever kills a mu'ahad will not even find the fragrance of Paradise, although its fragrance can be perceived from a distance of forty years' travel."""
"6458","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever kills a soul under covenant without right, Allah Almighty will make Paradise forbidden for him, to the extent that he will not even smell its fragrance."""
"6459","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever kills himself with a weapon, that same weapon will be in his hand and he will keep stabbing his stomach with it in the fire of Hell, abiding therein forever and ever. Whoever drinks poison and kills himself will keep sipping it in the fire of Hell, abiding therein forever and ever. And whoever throws himself off a mountain and kills himself will keep falling in the fire of Hell, abiding therein forever and ever."""
"6460","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever kills a gecko with the first blow, one hundred good deeds are recorded for him; whoever kills it with the second blow will receive such and such good deeds; and if he kills it with the third blow, he will receive such and such good deeds."""
"6461","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever is caused to die by an abdominal illness will not be punished in his grave."""
"6462","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever accuses his slave of fornication, the prescribed punishment (hadd) will be carried out on him on the Day of Resurrection, unless the slave turns out to be as he said."""
"6463","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever accuses his slave while the slave is innocent of what he said will be flogged as a prescribed punishment (hadd) on the Day of Resurrection, unless the slave turns out to be as he said."""
"6464","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever recites Ayat al-Kursi after every obligatory prayer, nothing will prevent him from entering Paradise except death."""
"6465","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever recites the last two verses of Surah al-Baqarah at night, they will suffice him."""
"6466","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever recites Surah al-Kafirun, it is equal for him to a quarter of the Qur'an, and whoever recites Surah al-Ikhlas, it is equal for him to a third of the Qur'an."""
"6467","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever recites the Qur'an, let him ask Allah alone through it, for soon there will come people who will recite the Qur'an and ask people (for worldly things) through it."""
"6468","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever recites one hundred verses in a night, the reward of standing in prayer for a night is recorded for him."""
"6469","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever recites one letter of the Book of Allah receives one good deed for it, and one good deed is equal to ten like it. I do not say that 'Alif Lam Mim' is one letter; rather, Alif is a letter, Lam is a letter and Mim is a letter."""
"6470","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever recites Surah al-Kahf on the day of Friday, light is made to shine for him between the two Fridays."""
"6471","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever recites Surah al-Kahf on the day of Friday, light is made to shine between him and the Ancient House (the Ka'bah)."""
"6472","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever recites Surah al-Ikhlas eleven times, Allah Almighty builds a house for him in Paradise."""
"6473","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever recites Surah al-Ikhlas, it is as if he has recited a third of the Qur'an."""
"6474","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever combines his Hajj and his Umrah (performs Hajj Qiran), one tawaf will suffice for both of them."""
"6475","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever severs the ties of kinship or swears a false oath will see its evil consequence before he dies."""
"6476","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever cuts down a lote tree, Allah Almighty will plunge his head headlong into the Fire."""
"6477","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever sits in a gathering and does not remember Allah in it, it will be a source of regret (loss) for him from Allah; and whoever lies down in a place and does not remember Allah in it, that too will be a source of regret for him from Allah."""
"6478","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever makes a contract of emancipation (mukatabah) with his slave for one hundred uqiyah, and the slave pays all of it except ten uqiyah and then becomes unable to pay, he remains a slave."""
"6479","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever's last words are 'La ilaha illallah' (there is no true god except Allah) will enter Paradise."""
"6480","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever has a covenant with a people should neither strengthen it further nor break it until its term expires, or until he notifies them, on equal terms, that the covenant is ended."""
"6481","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever has to swear an oath should swear only by Allah."""
"6482","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever has slaughtered his sacrificial animal before the prayer should slaughter another in its place, and whoever has not yet slaughtered should slaughter in the name of Allah."""
"6483","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever offered his sacrifice before the prayer should do it again."""
"6484","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever is gentle-natured, easygoing and soft-hearted, Allah Almighty will make the Fire forbidden for him."""
"6485","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever remains in the mosque waiting for the prayer is counted as being in prayer as long as his ablution (wudu) is not broken."""
"6486","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever is an agent working for us and has no wife, let him arrange a wife for himself; if he has no servant, let him arrange a servant; and if he has no house, let him arrange a house. Whoever acquires anything beyond that is a betrayer of trust or a thief."""
"6487","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever has an imam, the recitation of the imam counts as his recitation."""
"6488","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever has three daughters and is patient with them, and feeds them, gives them drink and clothes them according to his means, they will become a screen for him from the Fire on the Day of Resurrection."""
"6489","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever has a sacrificial animal to slaughter, when the crescent moon of Dhul-Hijjah is sighted, he should not cut his hair or his nails until he has offered his sacrifice."""
"6490","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever has the means and still does not offer a sacrifice should not come near our place of Eid prayer."""
"6491","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever has a partner in an orchard should not sell his share until he has offered it to his partner."""
"6492","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever has a partner in a dwelling or a date-palm orchard should not sell it until he has informed his partner; if he is pleased, he may take it, and if he dislikes it, he may leave it."""
"6493","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever has hair on his head should take good care of it."""
"6494","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever has wealth, its effect should be visible on him."""
"6495","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever has a date-palm orchard or land should not sell it until he has offered it to his partner."""
"6496","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever has two faces in this world (i.e. is a hypocrite) will have two tongues of fire on the Day of Resurrection."""
"6497","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever has a spare mount beyond his need should give it to someone who has no mount, and whoever has spare provisions beyond his need should give them to someone who has no provisions."""
"6498","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever among you has the means should marry, for it is more effective in lowering the gaze and guarding the private parts; and whoever does not have the means should fast, for it is a protection for him."""
"6499","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever among you wishes to offer voluntary prayer after the Friday prayer should pray four rak'ahs."""
"6500","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, then when he witnesses a matter, let him speak good or remain silent. And treat women well, for woman was created from a rib, and the most crooked part of the rib is its upper part; if you try to straighten it, you will break it, and if you leave it, it will remain crooked. So treat women well."""
"6501","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should treat his neighbour well; whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should honour his guest; and whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should speak good or remain silent."""
"6502","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should honour his guest. His special hospitality is one day and night, and hospitality is three days; whatever is beyond that is charity. It is not permissible for the guest to stay so long that he burdens his host until he is compelled to make him leave."""
"6503","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should take nothing except like for like, that is, gold for gold."""
"6504","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should not harm his neighbour. And treat women well."""
"6505","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should not enter the bathhouse without a waist-wrapper."""
"6506","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should not enter the bathhouse without a waist-wrapper; whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should not allow his wife to go into the bathhouse; and whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should not sit at a table where wine is being passed around."""
"6507","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should not pour his water onto another man's crop (i.e. he should not have intercourse with a pregnant slave-woman); whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should not have intercourse with a captive woman until he has established her istibra' (that she is not pregnant); whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should not sell anything from the spoils of war until it has been distributed; whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should not ride an animal from the fay' (public wealth) of the Muslims so that, when he has worn it down, he returns it to it; and whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should not wear a garment from the fay' of the Muslims so that, when he has worn it out, he returns it to it."""
"6508","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should not, by having intercourse with a pregnant slave-woman, give his water to another man's child."""
"6509","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should not wear silk or gold."""
"6510","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever makes the Hereafter his concern, Allah Almighty places his self-sufficiency in his heart, gathers his scattered affairs for him, and the world comes to him humbled. And whoever makes this world his concern, Allah Almighty places his poverty before his eyes, scatters his affairs, and he receives nothing of this world except what has been decreed for him."""
"6511","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever has wronged his brother in his honour or his wealth should seek his forgiveness today, before the Day comes when there will be neither dinar nor dirham. If he has good deeds, they will be taken from him in proportion to his wrongdoing; and if he has no good deeds, some of his companion's sins will be taken and placed upon him."""
"6512","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever has land and wishes to sell it should first offer it to his neighbour."""
"6513","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever has land should cultivate it himself or let his brother cultivate it, and he should not rent it out for a third, a quarter, or a fixed amount of grain."""
"6514","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever has land should cultivate it; if he cannot cultivate it and is unable to do so, he should give it to his Muslim brother free of charge and not rent it out to him. If he does not do that, he should keep his land (unused)."""
"6515","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever has two wives and inclines towards one of them will come on the Day of Resurrection with one of his sides leaning."""
"6516","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever makes the Hereafter his concern, Allah Almighty gathers his scattered affairs for him, places his self-sufficiency in his heart, and the world comes to him humbled. And whoever makes this world his concern, Allah Almighty scatters his affairs, places his poverty before his eyes, and he receives nothing of this world except what Allah Almighty has written for him."""
"6517","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever conceals knowledge from those who are entitled to it will be bridled with a bridle of fire on the Day of Resurrection."""
"6518","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever suppresses his anger while he is able to act upon it, Allah Almighty will call him on the Day of Resurrection before all of creation, until He lets him choose from the wide-eyed houris whichever of them he wishes to marry."""
"6519","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever deliberately lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire."""
"6520","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever lies about his dream will be made, on the Day of Resurrection, to tie a knot in a barley grain."""
"6521","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever suffers a broken bone, falls ill or becomes lame is released from ihram, and he must perform another Hajj the following year."""
"6522","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever suppresses his anger while he is able to act upon it, Allah Almighty will call him on the Day of Resurrection before all of creation, until He lets him choose from the wide-eyed houris whichever of them he wishes to marry."""
"6523","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever I am the mawla (friend and patron) of, Ali is also his mawla."""
"6524","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever I am the wali of, Ali is also his wali."""
"6525","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever wears silk in this world will not wear it in the Hereafter."""
"6526","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever wears a garment of fame (for show), Allah Almighty will clothe him on the Day of Resurrection in a garment like it and then set it ablaze with fire."""
"6527","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever slaps his slave or beats him, his expiation is to set him free."""
"6528","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever plays nard (a game of gambling), it is as though he has dipped his hand in the flesh and blood of swine."""
"6529","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever plays nard has disobeyed Allah and His Messenger."""
"6530","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever says something about divorce or freeing a slave, even in jest, it will take effect as he said."""
"6531","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever meets Allah without associating anything with Him will enter Paradise."""
"6532","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Who will deal with Ka'b bin al-Ashraf? For he has indeed harmed Allah and His Messenger."""
"6533","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever does not trim his moustache is not one of us."""
"6534","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever does not make the intention to fast before the break of dawn has no fast."""
"6535","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever does not make the intention to fast during the night has no fast."""
"6536","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever cannot find sandals should wear leather socks and cut them below the ankles."""
"6537","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever (in the state of ihram) cannot find sandals should wear leather socks, and whoever cannot find a waist-wrapper should wear trousers."""
"6538","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever does not firmly resolve to fast before dawn has no fast."""
"6539","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever does not give up false speech and acting upon it, Allah Almighty has no need of his giving up his food and drink."""
"6540","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever does not show mercy to our young and does not recognise the right of our elders is not one of us."""
"6541","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever does not thank people has not thanked Allah."""
"6542","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever has not prayed the two sunnah rak'ahs of Fajr, let him pray them after the sun rises."""
"6543","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whatever state a person dies in, Allah Almighty will raise him in that same state."""
"6544","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever dies while guarding the frontier in the way of Allah, Allah Almighty will continue for him the good deeds that he used to do, will also continue his provision, will keep him safe from the angels who test, and will raise him on the Day of Resurrection safe from terror."""
"6545","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever dies while guarding the frontier in the way of Allah, Allah Almighty will keep him safe from the trial of the grave."""
"6546","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever dies while he owes a dinar or a dirham as a debt, then there will be neither dinar nor dirham there; rather, it will be paid from his good deeds."""
"6547","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever dies while he still owes fasts, his guardian should fast on his behalf."""
"6548","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever dies without having fought in jihad and without having even thought of jihad in his heart has died upon a branch of hypocrisy."""
"6549","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever dies while he is addicted to wine will meet Allah as though he were an idol-worshipper."""
"6550","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever dies without having associated anyone with Allah will enter Paradise."""
"6551","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever dies without having associated anyone with Allah will enter Paradise, and whoever dies having associated anyone with Allah will enter the Fire."""
"6552","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever dies knowing that 'La ilaha illallah' (there is no true god except Allah) will enter Paradise."""
"6553","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever fiddles with the pebbles has done something idle."""
"6554","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever touches his private part, let him perform ablution (wudu)."""
"6555","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever touches his private part, let him perform ablution (wudu)."""
"6556","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever walks to an obligatory prayer in congregation, it is like a Hajj; and whoever walks to a voluntary prayer, it is like a voluntary Umrah."""
"6557","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever comes to own a relative within the prohibited degrees (mahram), that relative becomes free."""
"6558","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever lends out a milk-giving animal, it is charity in the morning and charity in the evening, both its morning milk and its evening milk."""
"6559","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever gives someone a goodly loan, or lends out a milk-giving animal, or gifts a waterskin, it is equal to freeing a slave."""
"6560","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever withholds surplus water or pasture, Allah Almighty will withhold His bounty from him on the Day of Resurrection."""
"6561","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever sleeps through his fixed night-time portion of recitation, or some part of it, and then recites it between the Fajr prayer and the Zuhr prayer, Allah Almighty will record it for him as though he had recited it during the night."""
"6562","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever sleeps through his Witr prayer or forgets it, let him pray it when he remembers it."""
"6563","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever sleeps through his Witr prayer, let him pray it when morning comes."""
"6564","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever goes to sleep with grease on his hand and does not wash it, and then some harm befalls him, let him blame no one but himself."""
"6565","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever vows to obey Allah, let him obey Him; and whoever vows to disobey Allah, let him not disobey Him."""
"6566","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever is struck by a need and presents it before people, his need will not be met; and whoever is struck by a need and presents it before Allah, Allah Almighty will soon grant him provision, sooner or later."""
"6567","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever stops at a place and says: I seek refuge in the perfect words of Allah from the evil of what He has created, nothing will harm him until he departs from there."""
"6568","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever forgets to send blessings upon me loses the way to Paradise."""
"6569","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever forgets a prayer, let him pray it when he remembers it, for Allah Almighty has said: Establish prayer for My remembrance."""
"6570","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever forgets something in his prayer, let him perform two prostrations while seated."""
"6571","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever forgets a prayer or sleeps and misses it, its expiation is that he prays it when he remembers it."""
"6572","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever forgets a prayer, let him pray it when he remembers it; there is no expiation for it other than that."""
"6573","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever, while fasting, forgetfully eats or drinks, let him complete his fast, for it is Allah Almighty who has fed him and given him drink."""
"6574","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever helps his brother in his absence, Allah Almighty will help him in this world and the Hereafter."""
"6575","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever helps his people unjustly is like a camel that falls into a well and is being pulled out by its tail."""
"6576","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever grants respite to his debtor or forgives his debt will be in the shade of the Throne on the Day of Resurrection."""
"6577","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever relieves a believer of one of the hardships of this world, Allah Almighty will relieve him of one of the hardships of the Day of Resurrection; whoever makes things easy for someone in difficulty, Allah Almighty will make things easy for him in this world and the Hereafter; whoever conceals the faults of a Muslim, Allah Almighty will conceal his faults in this world and the Hereafter; and Allah Almighty remains in the aid of a servant as long as the servant remains in the aid of his brother. Whoever travels a path seeking knowledge, Allah Almighty makes easy for him a path to Paradise. Whenever a people gather in one of the houses of Allah, reciting the Book of Allah and studying it among themselves, tranquility descends upon them, mercy covers them, the angels surround them, and Allah Almighty mentions them among those who are with Him. And whoever is held back by his deeds will not be advanced by his lineage."""
"6578","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever is scrutinised closely in the reckoning will be punished."""
"6579","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever is scrutinised closely in the reckoning is ruined."""
"6580","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever is wailed over is punished because of that wailing."""
"6581","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever cuts off his brother for a year, it is like shedding his blood."""
"6582","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Who is this who is cursing his camel?! Get down from it, and do not keep anything cursed with us. Do not invoke evil upon yourselves, do not invoke evil upon your children, and do not invoke evil upon your wealth, lest your invocation coincide with that hour from Allah in which something is asked and it is granted."""
"6583","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever finds dates, let him break his fast with them; and whoever does not, let him break his fast with water, for it is purifying."""
"6584","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever finds an animal whose owners were unable to feed it and so abandoned it, and he takes it, raises it and keeps it alive, then that animal becomes his."""
"6585","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever has the means, let him use a striped Yemeni cloth for his shroud."""
"6586","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever finds a lost item, let him take upright witnesses, and let him neither conceal it nor tamper with it. Then, if its owner is found, let him return it to him; otherwise, it is the wealth of Allah, which He gives to whomever He wills."""
"6587","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever experiences this whispering, let him say three times: We believe in Allah and His Messenger, and it will go away from him."""
"6588","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whomever you find committing bestiality with an animal, kill him and kill the animal as well."""
"6589","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whomever you find doing the deed of the people of Lut, kill both the one who does it and the one to whom it is done."""
"6590","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever joins a row, Allah Almighty will join him (with His mercy); and whoever cuts off a row, Allah Almighty will cut him off."""
"6591","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever put down wine (the rest of this sentence is missing in the source), and whoever became addicted to drinking it will be given khabal (the discharge from the wounds of the people of Hell) to drink."""
"6592","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever tramples upon the edge of his lower garment out of arrogance, dragging it along the ground, will be trampled in Hellfire."""
"6593","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whomever Allah Almighty protects from the evil of what is between his two jaws (the tongue) and the evil of what is between his two legs (the private parts) will enter Paradise."""
"6594","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever takes up the office of judge (qada') has, as it were, been slaughtered without a knife."""
"6595","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever is given authority over any of the affairs of the Muslims and screens himself off from their needs, wants, poverty and destitution, Allah Almighty will screen Himself from him on the Day of Resurrection and turn away from his need, want, destitution and poverty."""
"6596","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever among you holds an office and Allah Almighty intends good for him, He appoints for him a righteous adviser: if he forgets, he reminds him, and if he remembers, he helps him."""
"6597","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever does not show mercy to people, Allah Almighty will not show mercy to him either."""
"6598","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever does not show mercy is not shown mercy."""
"6599","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever does not show mercy is not shown mercy, and whoever does not forgive is not forgiven."""
"6600","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever does not show mercy is not shown mercy, whoever does not forgive is not forgiven, and whoever does not repent, his repentance is not accepted."""
"6601","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever does not thank people does not thank Allah."""
"6602","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever among your servants suits you, feed him from what you eat and clothe him from what you wear; and whoever does not suit you, sell him, but do not torment the creation of Allah."""
"6603","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever guarantees me one thing, I guarantee him Paradise: that he does not ask people for anything."""
"6604","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever guarantees me that he will not ask people for anything, I guarantee him Paradise."""
"6605","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever guarantees me his tongue and his private parts, I guarantee him Paradise."""
"6606","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever is deprived of gentleness is deprived of all good."""
"6607","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever violates my covenant of protection, I will be his opponent, and whomever I oppose, I will defeat."""
"6608","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever enters Paradise will live there in lasting bliss; he will never be in hardship, his clothes will not wear out, and his youth will not come to an end."""
"6609","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever shows off, Allah Almighty will disgrace him, and whoever acts to be heard of, Allah Almighty will disgrace him."""
"6610","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When Allah Almighty intends good for someone, He afflicts him with trials."""
"6611","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When Allah Almighty intends good for someone, He grants him understanding of the religion."""
"6612","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When Allah Almighty intends good for someone, He grants him understanding of the religion. I am only the one who distributes, and it is Allah who gives. This Ummah will always remain established upon the command of Allah; those who oppose them will not harm them, until the command of Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, comes."""
"6613","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever seeks the humiliation of Quraysh, Allah Almighty will humiliate him."""
"6614","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever makes things easy for someone in hardship, Allah Almighty will make things easy for him in this world and the Hereafter."""
"6615","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever among you drinks nabidh, let him drink it made from raisins alone, or from dates alone, or from unripe dates alone."""
"6616","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever climbs the mountain pass of al-Murar (Thaniyyat al-Murar), the sins will be removed from him that were removed from the Children of Israel."""
"6617","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever guarantees me his tongue and his private parts, I guarantee him Paradise."""
"6618","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Who then would obey Allah if I disobeyed Him?! Allah Almighty has entrusted me over all the people of the earth, and you do not trust me?! Indeed, from the offspring of this man will come a people who recite the Qur'an, but it will not go beyond their throats. They will pass out of the religion as an arrow passes through the game. They will kill the people of Islam and leave the idol-worshippers alone. If I were to find them, I would kill them as the people of 'Ad were killed."""
"6619","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever is engaged in fulfilling his brother's need, Allah Almighty will be engaged in fulfilling his need."""
"6620","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Mina is the resting place of whoever arrives first."""
"6621","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""This pulpit of mine stands upon one of the gates of Paradise."""
"6622","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Our halting place tomorrow, if Allah wills (in sha' Allah), will be at Khayf Bani Kinanah, where they swore oaths to one another upon disbelief."""
"6623","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Iraq will withhold its dirham and its measure (qafiz), Syria will withhold its mudd and its dinar, and Egypt will withhold its ardab and its dinar; and you will return to where you began, you will return to where you began, you will return to where you began."""
"6624","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Two greedy people are never satisfied: the seeker of knowledge and the seeker of the world."""
"6625","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Stop! Take upon yourselves only as many deeds as you are able to, for by Allah, Allah Almighty does not grow weary until you grow weary."""
"6626","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Stop, O Aishah! Allah Almighty does not like obscenity nor the deliberate use of obscenity."""
"6627","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Gently, O Aishah! Hold to gentleness, and beware of harshness and obscenity."""
"6628","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Wait, O Khalid! Do not revile her. By the One in whose hand is my soul, she has repented with such a repentance that if an unjust tax collector were to repent like it, he would be forgiven."""
"6629","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The miqat of the people of Madinah is Dhul-Hulayfah, and for those of the other route it is al-Juhfah; the miqat of the people of Iraq is Dhat Irq, that of the people of Najd is Qarn, and that of the people of Yemen is Yalamlam."""
"6630","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Our mawali (freed slaves) are from among us."""
"6631","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Sudden death is a seizure of wrath from Allah."""
"6632","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Barren (uncultivated) land belongs to Allah and His Messenger; so whoever revives any of it, it becomes his."""
"6633","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Musa bin Imran (peace be upon him) is the chosen (elect) servant of Allah."""
"6634","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The place of the lower garment is down to the middle of the shins and the calf muscle; if you refuse, then lower than that; and if you still refuse, then down behind the shin; but the ankles have no right to the lower garment."""
"6635","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A space the size of a whip in Paradise is better than the world and everything in it."""
"6636","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Standing for one hour in the path of Allah is better than standing in prayer on the Night of Decree (Laylat al-Qadr) beside the Black Stone."""
"6637","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The mawla (freed slave or ally) of a people is from among themselves."""
"6638","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The most blessed of horses are those of a reddish (chestnut) colour."""
"6639","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The dead animals of the sea are lawful, and its water is purifying."""
"6640","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Water is purifying; nothing makes it impure."""
"6641","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Nothing makes water impure."""
"6642","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The one who becomes seasick at sea and vomits receives the reward of one martyr, and the one who drowns receives the reward of two martyrs."""
"6643","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The mu'adhdhin is forgiven as far as his voice reaches, and his reward is equal to the reward of those who pray with him."""
"6644","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The mu'adhdhin is forgiven as far as his voice reaches, and every moist and dry thing bears witness for him; and for the one who attends the prayer, twenty-five prayers are recorded, and the sins between them are expiated for him."""
"6645","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The mu'adhdhins will have the longest necks of all people on the Day of Resurrection."""
"6646","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The mu'adhdhins are the trustees of the Muslims in the matter of their prayer and their needs."""
"6647","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The mu'adhdhins are the trustees of the Muslims in the matter of their iftar and their suhur."""
"6648","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A believer is the brother of a believer, so it is not lawful for a believer to make a bargain over his brother's bargain, nor to propose marriage over his brother's proposal, until he gives it up."""
"6649","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When the believer desires a child in Paradise, its conception, birth and growth to full age will be completed in a single moment, just as he desires."""
"6650","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The strong believer is better and more beloved to Allah Almighty than the weak believer, though there is good in both. Be eager for what benefits you, seek help from Allah and do not give up. If something befalls you, do not say, 'If only I had done such-and-such, it would have been such-and-such.' Rather say, 'Allah decreed it, and He did what He willed,' for saying 'if' opens the door to the work of Satan."""
"6651","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The believer who mixes with people and bears their harm patiently is better than the believer who does not mix with people and does not bear their harm patiently."""
"6652","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The believer is in a state of good in every condition, so much so that when his soul is drawn out from between his sides, he is praising Allah."""
"6653","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The believer is guileless and noble, while the wicked person is cunning and base."""
"6654","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The believer to the believer is like a building, one part of which strengthens another."""
"6655","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The believer is the mirror of the believer."""
"6656","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The believer is the mirror of the believer, and the believer is the brother of the believer; he protects him from loss and guards him in his absence."""
"6657","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The believer keeps having his sins expiated through afflictions."""
"6658","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The believer is the one from whom people are safe regarding their wealth and their lives, and the emigrant (muhajir) is the one who abandons sins and wrongdoings."""
"6659","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The believer among the people of faith is like the head in the body; the believer feels pain for the people of faith just as the body feels the pain of the head."""
"6660","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The believer eats with the capacity of one intestine, whereas the disbeliever eats with the capacity of seven intestines."""
"6661","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The believer is sociable, and there is no good in a person who neither gets along with others nor is gotten along with."""
"6662","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The believer gets along with others and others get along with him, and there is no good in a person who neither gets along with others nor is gotten along with; and the best of people is the one who is most beneficial to people."""
"6663","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The believer drinks with the capacity of one intestine, whereas the disbeliever drinks with the capacity of seven intestines."""
"6664","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The believer feels protective jealousy (ghayrah), and Allah Almighty is the most intense in protective jealousy."""
"6665","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The believer dies with sweat on his forehead."""
"6666","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The blood of the believers is equal; they are one hand against those besides them, and even the lowest of them may grant protection on their behalf. Beware! A believer is not to be killed in retaliation for a disbeliever, nor one under a covenant during the term of his covenant. Whoever commits a crime, it is upon himself; and whoever commits a crime or shelters a criminal, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels and all the people."""
"6667","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The believers are like one body; if its head aches, the rest of the whole body joins it in fever and sleeplessness."""
"6668","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The believers are like one body; if its head aches, the whole body feels the pain, and if its eye aches, the whole body feels the pain."""
"6669","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The believers are gentle and soft-natured, like the camel with a nose-rein: if it is led, it follows, and if it is made to kneel even on a rock, it kneels."""
"6670","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The one who is skilled in the Qur'an will be with the noble and righteous scribe angels, and the one who recites it stammering, finding it difficult, will have a double reward."""
"6671","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The invitations of two people who host feasts out of pride and rivalry are not to be accepted, nor is their food to be eaten."""
"6672","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The seller and the buyer both have the option (to cancel) as long as they have not separated, unless the transaction was made with a stipulated option; and it is not lawful for one to leave his companion for fear that he might ask to cancel the transaction."""
"6673","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The seller and the buyer both have the option (to cancel) as long as they have not separated, unless the sale was made with a stipulated option; and if the sale was made with a stipulated option, the sale becomes binding."""
"6674","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Each of the seller and the buyer has the option over the other as long as they have not separated, except in a sale with a stipulated option."""
"6675","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The one who falsely claims to have what he has not been given is like one who wears two garments of falsehood."""
"6676","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The one who holds firmly to my Sunnah at the time of my Ummah's disagreement is like one who holds a live coal in his hand."""
"6677","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The woman whose husband has died should not wear clothes dyed with safflower (yellow), nor clothes dyed with red ochre, nor jewellery; nor should she apply henna, nor apply kohl."""
"6678","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Gatherings are a trust (what is said in them is confidential)."""
"6679","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The mujahid is the one who strives against his own self for the sake of Allah."""
"6680","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The woman in ihram should neither wear a face veil (niqab) nor gloves."""
"6681","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The women who seek khul' (separation at their own request) are the hypocrites."""
"6682","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The defendant has the greater right to take the oath, unless evidence is established against him."""
"6683","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Madinah is a sanctuary from Ayr to Thawr. Whoever introduces an innovation in it or shelters an innovator, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels and all the people; Allah Almighty will not accept from him on the Day of Resurrection any voluntary deed or obligatory one. The protection of the Muslims is one, and even the lowest of them may grant it; so whoever violates the protection of a Muslim, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels and all the people; Allah Almighty will not accept from him on the Day of Resurrection any voluntary deed or obligatory one. And whoever attributes his lineage to other than his father, or ascribes himself to other than his mawali, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels and all the people; Allah Almighty will not accept from him on the Day of Resurrection any voluntary deed or obligatory one."""
"6684","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Madinah is a sanctuary from Ayr to Thawr. Its grass is not to be cut, its game is not to be disturbed, and its lost property is not to be picked up except by one who announces it. It is not proper for a man to carry weapons in it for fighting, nor is it proper for any of its trees to be cut, except that a man may cut to feed his camel."""
"6685","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Madinah is a sanctuary from such-and-such a place to such-and-such a place. Its trees are not to be cut, nor is any innovation to be introduced in it. Whoever introduces an innovation in it or shelters an innovator, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels and all the people; Allah Almighty will not accept from him on the Day of Resurrection any voluntary deed or obligatory one."""
"6686","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Madinah is a safe sanctuary."""
"6687","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Disputing about the Qur'an is disbelief."""
"6688","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A person is counted as being in prayer as long as he is waiting for it."""
"6689","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A person will be with the one he loves."""
"6690","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A woman is to be covered; when she goes out of the house, Satan eyes her."""
"6691","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A woman belongs to the last of her husbands."""
"6692","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The whole of Muzdalifah is a place of standing."""
"6693","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Mizr (barley liquor), all of it, is unlawful."""
"6694","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Asking in supplication is that you raise your hands level with your shoulders; seeking forgiveness is that you point with one finger; and ibtihal (imploring humbly) is that you stretch out both your hands fully."""
"6695","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Begging from people is scratches with which a man scars his own face; so whoever wishes may preserve his face, and whoever wishes may leave it, except that a man asks one in authority, or asks in a matter for which he finds no alternative."""
"6696","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Two people who revile each other are two devils who speak obscenities to each other and lie against each other."""
"6697","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whatever two people who revile each other say, its sin is upon the one who began it, unless the wronged one exceeds the limit."""
"6698","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A woman with istihadah (irregular bleeding) should leave the prayer during the days of her menstrual periods, then take a ritual bath (ghusl) and pray, and perform ablution (wudu) at the time of every prayer."""
"6699","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A woman with istihadah (irregular bleeding) should take a ritual bath once from one menstrual period to the next."""
"6700","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The one whose counsel is sought is entrusted."""
"6701","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The mosque whose foundation was laid on piety is this mosque of mine."""
"6702","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The mosque is the house of every believer."""
"6703","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Musk is the best of perfumes."""
"6704","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A Muslim is the brother of a Muslim."""
"6705","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A Muslim is the brother of a Muslim, and it is not lawful for a Muslim to sell his brother anything that has a defect unless he makes it clear to him."""
"6706","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A Muslim is the brother of a Muslim; he does not betray him, nor lie to him, nor forsake him. Everything of a Muslim is sacred to another Muslim: his honour, his wealth and his blood. Piety is here - and he (peace and blessings be upon him) pointed to the heart - it is enough evil for a man that he looks down upon his Muslim brother."""
"6707","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A Muslim is the brother of a Muslim; he does not wrong him, nor forsake him. Whoever is engaged in fulfilling his brother's need, Allah Almighty will be engaged in fulfilling his need; whoever relieves a Muslim of a hardship, Allah Almighty will relieve him, because of it, of one of the hardships of the Day of Resurrection; and whoever conceals a Muslim's faults, Allah Almighty will conceal his faults on the Day of Resurrection."""
"6708","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a Muslim is questioned in the grave, he testifies 'La ilaha illallah wa anna Muhammadan rasulullah' (There is no true god except Allah, and Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) is the Messenger of Allah), and this is the meaning of the saying of Allah Almighty: Allah Almighty keeps firm those who believe with the firm word in the life of this world and in the Hereafter."""
"6709","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A Muslim is the one from whose tongue and hand the other Muslims are safe."""
"6710","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A Muslim is the one from whose tongue and hand the other Muslims are safe, and a believer is the one whom people trust with their lives and their wealth."""
"6711","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A Muslim is the one from whose tongue and hand the other Muslims are safe, and an emigrant (muhajir) is the one who abandons what Allah has forbidden."""
"6712","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The blood of the Muslims is equal (in relation to one another). Even the lowest of them may grant protection (to someone), which is binding on all of them, and even the most distant of them may grant protection on their behalf. They are like one hand against others. The strong among them will return (the share) to their weak, and the swift to the one who stays behind. A believer is not to be killed in retaliation for a disbeliever, nor is one under a covenant to be killed during the term of his covenant."""
"6713","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Muslims are partners in three things: in pasture, in water and in fire."""
"6714","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Muslims are bound by their conditions."""
"6715","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Muslims are bound by their conditions, provided they concern what is lawful."""
"6716","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Muslims are bound by their conditions, so long as they are in accordance with the truth."""
"6717","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Calamities, illnesses and griefs in this world are a recompense (for sins)."""
"6718","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A woman who has been divorced three times has neither housing nor maintenance."""
"6719","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The one who transgresses in (collecting) charity is like the one who withholds it."""
"6720","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Maghrib is the witr of the day, so make the night prayer witr (odd-numbered) as well."""
"6721","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Praised Station (al-Maqam al-Mahmud) means the intercession."""
"6722","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A mukatab (a slave who has made a contract to pay money in exchange for his freedom) remains a slave as long as even one dirham of his contract remains outstanding."""
"6723","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A mukatab is freed in proportion to what he has paid; the prescribed punishment (hadd) will be applied to him in proportion to how much of him has been freed; and he will inherit in proportion to how much of him has been freed."""
"6724","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Those who amass much wealth will be the lowest in rank on the Day of Resurrection."""
"6725","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Scheming and deception (lead) to the Fire."""
"6726","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Scheming, deception and betrayal (lead) to the Fire."""
"6727","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The angels keep praying for each one of you as long as he remains in the place where he prayed, so long as he does not lose his ablution or get up and leave: 'O Allah, forgive him; O Allah, have mercy on him.'"""
"6728","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The angels are Allah's witnesses in the heavens, and you are Allah's witnesses on the earth."""
"6729","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Kingship is in Quraysh, judgeship is in the Ansar, the call to prayer (adhan) is in the Abyssinians, and trustworthiness is in (the tribe of) Azd."""
"6730","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""One who wears sandals is in the position of one who is riding."""
"6731","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""One who wears sandals is (like) one riding."""
"6732","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A minhah (an animal lent out for use) is to be returned, and people are bound by their conditions so long as they are in accordance with the truth."""
"6733","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The one who spends on horses in the path of Allah is like one who keeps his hands stretched out in giving charity and does not withdraw them."""
"6734","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Mahdi will be from my offspring, from the descendants of Fatimah."""
"6735","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Mahdi will be from us, the People of the House (Ahl al-Bayt); Allah Almighty will rectify him in a single night."""
"6736","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Mahdi will be from me; he will have a broad forehead and a slightly raised nose. He will fill the earth with equity and justice just as it will have been filled with tyranny and oppression, and he will rule for seven years."""
"6737","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Scale (the balance) is in the Hand of Allah, the Most Merciful; He raises some peoples and lowers others."""
"6738","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The one who dies of pleurisy (dhat al-janb) is a martyr."""
"6739","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The deceased will be raised in the same clothes in which he died."""
"6740","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The deceased is punished because of the wailing of the living, when they say: 'Alas, my support! Alas, the one who clothed me! Alas, my helper! Alas, my mountain!' and words like these; he is shaken and it is said: 'Were you like that?! Were you like that?!'"""
"6741","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The deceased is punished in his grave because of the lamentation made over him."""
